IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cbca-core`
IMPORT `cb1-nouns`
IMPORT `cb1-part1-application`
IMPORT `cb1-part2-incorporation`
IMPORT `cb1-part3-capacity`
IMPORT `cb1-part4-records`
IMPORT `cb1-part4-isc-register`
IMPORT `cb1-part5-shares`
IMPORT `cb1-part5-own-shares`
IMPORT `cb1-part5-capital-dividends`
IMPORT `cb1-part6-constrained-shares`

-- Canada Business Corporations Act (R.S.C. 1985, c. C-44), sections 1 and 3 to 47 -- THE SEAT LAYER.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. The layer-1 modules were encoded from a plain-text rendering of the Justice Canada
-- consolidation current to 2026-09-30, which is not an official version; nothing here is verified against
-- the official text.
--
-- SEAT: a person who incorporates, directs or holds shares in a corporation under the Act: an incorporator,
-- a director or officer, or a shareholder (including a minority shareholder), asking what the Act lets them
-- do, what it requires of them, what they may require of the corporation, and what can be done to them.
-- There is no seat for the Director, a court or any other official: where the Act gives an official a
-- power over the person, the question is "what can the Director (or a court) do to me?".
--
-- This layer phrases the rules already encoded in the layer-1 modules imported above as the questions that
-- person would ask. Nothing here is new law, and no rule is restated: every question calls a layer-1 rule.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS. Every question takes plain inputs -- yes/no, numbers, dates, text, and the modules' own
-- choices -- one for each fact the person can state, each with an @desc worded as that person would be asked.
-- The records the layer-1 rules expect (the articles, the registers, the solvency facts ...) are built inside
-- each question, in its WHERE, from those answers. A record field that the rule called never reads would
-- get a fixed placeholder, with a comment; every field that a rule reads is asked.
-- Where a layer-1 rule takes the answer of another layer-1 rule as an input (section 10(3), section 14,
-- section 25, section 34 and so on), the question asks the facts behind that answer and calls both rules,
-- so the person is not asked a legal conclusion.
-- A fact the Act leaves to the regulations (a prescribed period, a prescribed form) is a plain input.
--
-- PAIRED QUESTIONS (Hohfeld). Where the text gives the person a claim, privilege, power or immunity, the
-- facts about the other party on which the text makes it depend are asked; where the Act also puts a duty or
-- a liability on the person, there is a paired question ("What do I owe ...?", "What can be done to me ...?").
-- The pairs are listed in NOTES.md under "Jural relations".
--
-- FIGURES. The Act's own figures (two thirds in "special resolution", the two-year limits, the ten-year
-- vesting) are the rules' constants, never asked. Where the Act lets the regulations, the articles or the
-- Director substitute a figure, the figure is a plain input.
--
-- The headings below are in the text's own order. A group that only arises in a situation the person may not
-- be in (a share acquisition by the corporation, a sale of constrained shares) says so in its heading comment.

§ `Canada Business Corporations Act -- the questions of an incorporator, director, officer or shareholder`

§§ `Whether the Act applies to my corporation (Part I, s 3)`

-- s 3(1). The Act applies to every corporation incorporated, and every body corporate continued as a
-- corporation, under it, unless it has been discontinued under the Act.
@export Does the Act apply to my body corporate (s 3(1))?
GIVEN `it was incorporated under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your corporation incorporated under the Canada Business Corporations Act?
      `it was continued under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your body corporate continued as a corporation under the Canada Business Corporations Act?
      `it has been discontinued under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your body corporate been discontinued under the Canada Business Corporations Act?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the Act apply to my body corporate` IF
    `this Act applies to the body corporate within s 3(1)` `it was incorporated under the Act` `it was continued under the Act` `it has been discontinued under the Act`

-- s 3(3). Three laws do not apply to a corporation: the Canada Not-for-profit Corporations Act, the
-- Winding-up and Restructuring Act, and any provision of a Special Act (as defined in section 87 of the
-- Canada Transportation Act) that is inconsistent with this Act.
@export Is a law excluded from applying to my corporation (s 3(3))?
GIVEN `the law in question` IS A `Law that s 3(3) may exclude from applying to a corporation` @desc Which law are you asking about?
      -- out of range: section 87 of the Canada Transportation Act (outside the Act)
      `the Special Act provision is inconsistent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is a provision of a Special Act, is it inconsistent with the Canada Business Corporations Act?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is a law excluded from applying to my corporation` IF
    `the law is excluded from applying to a corporation within s 3(3)` `the law in question` `the Special Act provision is inconsistent`

-- s 3(4). No corporation may carry on the business of a bank, a cooperative credit association, an
-- insurance company or society, or a trust and loan company (each as governed by its own Act).
@export Is my corporation prohibited from carrying on this kind of business (s 3(4))?
GIVEN `the business` IS A `Business a corporation may not carry on under s 3(4)` @desc What kind of business do you want your corporation to carry on?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my corporation prohibited from carrying on this kind of business` IF
    `the corporation is prohibited from carrying on the business within s 3(4)` `the business`

-- s 3(5). No corporation may carry on business as a degree-granting educational institution unless a
-- federal or provincial agent that has by law the power to confer degree-granting authority has expressly
-- authorized it.
@export Is my corporation prohibited from carrying on business as a degree-granting educational institution (s 3(5))?
GIVEN `it would be a degree-granting educational institution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would your corporation carry on business as a degree-granting educational institution?
      `it has been expressly authorized` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a federal or provincial agent that by law has the power to confer degree-granting authority expressly authorized it to do so?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my corporation prohibited from carrying on a degree-granting educational institution` IF
    `the corporation is prohibited from carrying on a degree-granting educational institution within s 3(5)` `it would be a degree-granting educational institution` `it has been expressly authorized`

§§ `Incorporating (Part II, s 5 to s 9)`

-- s 5(1). One or more individuals or bodies corporate may incorporate a corporation by signing articles of
-- incorporation and complying with section 7 (sending the articles to the Director).
@export May we incorporate a corporation by signing these articles (s 5(1))?
GIVEN `the number of individuals who sign` IS A NUMBER @desc How many individuals will sign the articles of incorporation?
      `the number of bodies corporate that sign` IS A NUMBER @desc How many bodies corporate will sign the articles of incorporation?
      `every signing individual is qualified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is every individual who will sign at least 18 years old, not incapable and not an undischarged bankrupt?
      `we have complied with section 7` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the signers sent the articles and the required notices to the Director (section 7)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May we incorporate a corporation by signing these articles` IF
    `the signers may incorporate a corporation within s 5(1)` `the number of individuals who sign` `the number of bodies corporate that sign` `every signing individual is qualified` `we have complied with section 7`

-- s 5(2). An individual may incorporate a corporation only if they are at least 18, are not incapable, and
-- do not have the status of bankrupt. "Incapable" is defined in s 2(1): found unable to manage their
-- property under the law of a province (other than by reason of minority), or declared incapable by a
-- court outside Canada.
@export May I, as an individual, incorporate a corporation (s 5(2))?
GIVEN `my age in complete years` IS A NUMBER @desc How old are you, in complete years?
      `I have been found unable to manage my property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been found, under the law of a province, to be unable to manage your property?
      `that was by reason of my minority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, was that only because you are a minor?
      `a court outside Canada has declared me incapable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a court outside Canada declared you incapable?
      `I am a bankrupt` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have the status of a bankrupt?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I as an individual incorporate a corporation` IF
    `the individual may incorporate a corporation within s 5(2)` `my age in complete years` `I have been found unable to manage my property` `that was by reason of my minority` `a court outside Canada has declared me incapable` `I am a bankrupt`

-- s 6(1). The articles must follow the Director's form and set out the name, the province of the registered
-- office, the classes and any maximum number of shares (with the class rights where there are two or more
-- classes, and the directors' authority where a class may be issued in series), any restriction on the issue,
-- transfer or ownership of shares, the number (or minimum and maximum number) of directors, and any
-- restrictions on the businesses the corporation may carry on.
@export Are my articles of incorporation complete (s 6(1))?
GIVEN `my articles follow the Director's form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do your articles follow the form that the Director fixes?
      `my articles set out the name` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do your articles set out the name of the corporation?
      `my articles set out the province` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do your articles set out the province in Canada where the registered office is to be?
      `my articles set out the classes and maximum` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do your articles set out the classes of shares, and any maximum number of shares, the corporation may issue?
      `I will have two or more classes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Will the corporation have two or more classes of shares?
      `my articles set out the class rights` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do your articles set out the rights, privileges, restrictions and conditions attaching to each class?
      `a class may be issued in series` IS A BOOLEAN @desc May a class of shares be issued in series?
      `my articles set out the series authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do your articles set out the authority given to the directors to fix the number, designation and rights of the shares of each series?
      `I want to restrict shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the issue, transfer or ownership of the corporation's shares to be restricted?
      `my articles set out the restrictions on shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do your articles state that, and the nature of the restrictions?
      `my articles set out the number of directors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do your articles set out the number of directors?
      `my articles set out the minimum and maximum` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do your articles instead set out a minimum and a maximum number of directors?
      -- out of range: section 107 (piece cb2)
      `my articles rely on paragraph 107(a)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, does paragraph 107(a) allow a minimum and maximum number of directors for your corporation?
      `I want to restrict the businesses` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation to be restricted in the businesses it may carry on?
      `my articles set out the business restrictions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do your articles set out those restrictions?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are my articles of incorporation complete` IF
    `the articles of incorporation are complete within s 6(1)` `my articles`
    WHERE
        `my articles` MEANS `Articles of incorporation as delivered (s 6(1))` WITH
            `follow the form that the Director fixes` IS `my articles follow the Director's form`
            `set out the name of the corporation` IS `my articles set out the name`
            `set out the province in Canada where the registered office is to be situated` IS `my articles set out the province`
            `set out the classes and any maximum number of shares that the corporation is authorized to issue` IS `my articles set out the classes and maximum`
            `there will be two or more classes of shares` IS `I will have two or more classes`
            `set out the rights, privileges, restrictions and conditions attaching to each class of shares` IS `my articles set out the class rights`
            `a class of shares may be issued in series` IS `a class may be issued in series`
            `set out the authority given to the directors to fix the number of shares in, and to determine the designation of, and the rights, privileges, restrictions and conditions attaching to, the shares of each series` IS `my articles set out the series authority`
            `the issue, transfer or ownership of shares of the corporation is to be restricted` IS `I want to restrict shares`
            `set out a statement to that effect and a statement as to the nature of the restrictions` IS `my articles set out the restrictions on shares`
            `set out the number of directors` IS `my articles set out the number of directors`
            `set out the minimum and maximum number of directors` IS `my articles set out the minimum and maximum`
            `paragraph 107(a) allows a minimum and maximum number of directors` IS `my articles rely on paragraph 107(a)`
            `there are restrictions on the businesses that the corporation may carry on` IS `I want to restrict the businesses`
            `set out the restrictions on the businesses that the corporation may carry on` IS `my articles set out the business restrictions`

-- s 6(2). The articles may set out any provision that the Act or the law permits to be set out in the
-- by-laws.
@export May my articles set out this provision (s 6(2))?
GIVEN `the Act or the law permits it in the by-laws` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Act, or any other law, permit this provision to be set out in the by-laws of a corporation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my articles set out this provision` IF
    `the articles may set out the provision within s 6(2)` `the Act or the law permits it in the by-laws`

-- s 6(3). If the articles or a unanimous shareholder agreement require a greater number of votes of directors
-- or shareholders than the Act requires to effect an action, they prevail -- but the articles may not
-- require more votes than section 109 to remove a director (s 6(4)). The fraction is the share of the votes
-- needed.
@export What fraction of the votes is needed to effect this action (s 6(3))?
GIVEN `the fraction the Act requires` IS A NUMBER @desc What fraction of the votes does the Act require to effect the action (for example 0.5, or 0.6667 for two thirds)?
      `my articles require a different fraction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do your articles require a greater fraction of the votes?
      `the fraction my articles require` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, what fraction? (0 if they do not)
      `a unanimous shareholder agreement requires a different fraction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a unanimous shareholder agreement require a greater fraction of the votes?
      `the fraction the agreement requires` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, what fraction? (0 if it does not)
      `the action is removing a director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the action the removal of a director by the shareholders?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What fraction of the votes is needed to effect this action` IS
    `the fraction of the votes needed to effect the action within s 6(3)` `the fraction the Act requires` `the articles' fraction` `the agreement's fraction` `the action is removing a director`
    WHERE
        `the articles' fraction` MEANS IF `my articles require a different fraction` THEN JUST `the fraction my articles require` ELSE NOTHING
        `the agreement's fraction` MEANS IF `a unanimous shareholder agreement requires a different fraction` THEN JUST `the fraction the agreement requires` ELSE NOTHING

-- s 6(4). The articles may not require a greater number of votes of shareholders to remove a director than
-- section 109 requires.
@export May my articles require this fraction of the votes to remove a director (s 6(4))?
GIVEN `the fraction my articles would require` IS A NUMBER @desc What fraction of the shareholders' votes would your articles require to remove a director?
      -- out of range: section 109 (piece cb2)
      `the fraction section 109 requires` IS A NUMBER @desc What fraction of the shareholders' votes does section 109 of the Act require to remove a director?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my articles require this fraction of the votes to remove a director` IF
    `an articles requirement for the removal of a director is permitted within s 6(4)` `the fraction my articles would require` `the fraction section 109 requires`

-- s 7. An incorporator must send the Director the articles of incorporation and the notice of registered
-- office (section 19) and the notice of directors (section 106).
@export Have I, as an incorporator, sent what the Act requires to the Director (s 7)?
GIVEN `I sent the articles` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you sent the Director the articles of incorporation?
      `I sent the notice of registered office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you sent the Director the notice of registered office that section 19 requires?
      -- out of range: section 106 (piece cb2)
      `I sent the notice of directors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you sent the Director the notice of directors that section 106 requires?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I as an incorporator sent what the Act requires to the Director` IF
    `the incorporator has complied with the duty to send the articles and documents within s 7` `I sent the articles` `I sent the notice of registered office` `I sent the notice of directors`

-- s 8. On receipt of the articles the Director shall issue a certificate of incorporation, but may refuse
-- it if a notice required by s 19(2) or 106(1) shows that the corporation would not comply with the Act.
@export What will the Director do on receiving my articles (s 8)?
GIVEN `the Director has received my articles` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Director received your articles of incorporation?
      -- out of range: section 106(1) (piece cb2)
      `a notice shows I would not comply with the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a notice that you sent under subsection 19(2) or 106(1) show that the corporation, if it came into existence, would not comply with the Act?
GIVETH AN `Outcome of sending articles of incorporation under s 8`
DECIDE `What will the Director do on receiving my articles` IS
    `what the Director must or may do on receiving articles of incorporation within s 8` `the Director has received my articles` `a notice shows I would not comply with the Act`

-- s 9. A corporation comes into existence on the date shown in its certificate of incorporation.
@export Has my corporation come into existence on this day (s 9)?
GIVEN `the date shown in my certificate of incorporation` IS A DATE @desc What date is shown in your certificate of incorporation?
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you want to know whether it exists?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has my corporation come into existence on this day` IF
    `the corporation has come into existence by the day within s 9` `the date shown in my certificate of incorporation` `the day I am asking about`

§§ `My corporation's name (Part II, s 10 to s 13)`

-- s 10(1). The name of every corporation must contain, other than only in a figurative or descriptive sense,
-- one of "Limited", "Limitée", "Incorporated", "Incorporée", "Corporation" or "Société par actions de régime
-- fédéral" or the corresponding abbreviation ("Ltd.", "Ltée", "Inc.", "Corp.", "S.A.R.F.").
@export Does my corporation's name contain a word or abbreviation that the Act requires (s 10(1))?
GIVEN `the corporate word in my name` IS A STRING @desc Which corporate word or abbreviation does your corporation's name contain, used as part of the name and not only in a figurative or descriptive sense? (leave empty if none)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my corporation's name contain a required word` IF
    `the corporate name carries a required word within s 10(1)` (LIST `the corporate word in my name`)

-- s 10(1). A corporation may use and be legally designated by either the full or the corresponding
-- abbreviated form.
@export May my corporation use and be legally designated by this form of its name (s 10(1))?
GIVEN `the form my corporation uses` IS A STRING @desc Which form of the corporate word do you want to use (for example "Inc." or "Incorporated")?
      `the form in my corporation's name` IS A STRING @desc Which form of the corporate word does your corporation's name contain?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my corporation use and be legally designated by this form of its name` IF
    `the corporation may use and be legally designated by the form within s 10(1)` `the form my corporation uses` `the form in my corporation's name`

-- s 10(1), (1.1) and (2). The required word is a duty of every corporation, except a corporation whose name
-- before subsection 10(1.1) came into force had "Société commerciale canadienne" or "S.C.C." in it, and a
-- body corporate continued under the Act that the Director has exempted from subsection (1).
@export Must my corporation's name contain a required word (s 10(1), (1.1), (2))?
GIVEN
      -- out of range: the day subsection 10(1.1) came into force (not in the text)
      `my name had the S.C.C. expression` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Immediately before subsection 10(1.1) came into force, did your corporation's name include "Société commerciale canadienne" or "S.C.C." other than only in a figurative or descriptive sense?
      `my body corporate was continued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your body corporate continued as a corporation under the Act?
      `the Director has exempted it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Director exempted your body corporate from subsection 10(1)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my corporation's name contain a required word` IF
    `the corporation must carry a required word in its name within s 10(1), s 10(1.1) and s 10(2)` `my name had the S.C.C. expression` `my body corporate was continued` `the Director has exempted it`

-- s 10(1.1). A corporation that falls within the saving may use and be legally designated by either the
-- expression "Société commerciale canadienne" or the abbreviation "S.C.C.".
@export May my corporation use and be designated by the expression or abbreviation "Société commerciale canadienne" or "S.C.C." (s 10(1.1))?
GIVEN
      -- out of range: the day subsection 10(1.1) came into force (not in the text)
      `my name had the S.C.C. expression` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Immediately before subsection 10(1.1) came into force, did your corporation's name include "Société commerciale canadienne" or "S.C.C." other than only in a figurative or descriptive sense?
      `the expression I want to use` IS A STRING @desc Which expression or abbreviation do you want to use?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my corporation use and be designated by the S.C.C. expression` IF
    `the corporation may use and be legally designated by the expression or abbreviation within s 10(1.1)` `my name had the S.C.C. expression` `the expression I want to use`

-- s 10(3). Subject to section 12(1), the name may be set out in the articles in an English form, a French
-- form, an English form and a French form, or a combined English and French form, so long as the combined
-- form meets the prescribed criteria.
@export May I set out my corporation's name in the articles in this form (s 10(3))?
GIVEN `the form of name` IS A `Form of corporate name set out in the articles (s 10(3))` @desc Which form of the name do you want to set out in the articles?
      -- out of range: the regulations (not among the sources)
      `the combined form meets the criteria` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is a combined English and French form, does it meet the prescribed criteria?
      -- out of range: the regulations (not among the sources)
      `the name is prohibited` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the name prohibited by the regulations, or does it fail the prescribed requirements (section 12(1))?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I set out my corporation's name in the articles in this form` IF
    `the form of name may be set out in the articles within s 10(3)` `the form of name` `the combined form meets the criteria` `the name is prohibited`

-- s 10(3). The corporation may use and be legally designated by any such form.
@export May my corporation use and be legally designated by a form of its name set out in the articles (s 10(3))?
GIVEN `the form of name` IS A `Form of corporate name set out in the articles (s 10(3))` @desc Which form of the name do you want to use?
      -- out of range: the regulations (not among the sources)
      `the combined form meets the criteria` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is a combined English and French form, does it meet the prescribed criteria?
      -- out of range: the regulations (not among the sources)
      `the name is prohibited` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the name prohibited by the regulations, or does it fail the prescribed requirements (section 12(1))?
      `the form is set out in my articles` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that form set out in your corporation's articles?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my corporation use and be legally designated by a form of its name set out in the articles` IF
    `the corporation may use and be legally designated by the form within s 10(3)` (`the form of name may be set out in the articles within s 10(3)` `the form of name` `the combined form meets the criteria` `the name is prohibited`) `the form is set out in my articles`

-- s 10(4). Subject to section 12(1), a corporation may, for use outside Canada, set out its name in its
-- articles in any language form and use and be legally designated by that form outside Canada.
@export May my corporation use a language form of its name outside Canada (s 10(4))?
GIVEN `the name is set out in my articles in that form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the name set out in your articles in that language form for use outside Canada?
      `I use it outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Will you use that form outside Canada?
      -- out of range: the regulations (not among the sources)
      `the name is prohibited` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the name prohibited by the regulations, or does it fail the prescribed requirements (section 12(1))?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my corporation use a language form of its name outside Canada` IF
    `the corporation may use and be legally designated by the name outside Canada within s 10(4)` `the name is set out in my articles in that form` `I use it outside Canada` `the name is prohibited`

-- s 10(5). A corporation shall set out its name in legible characters in all contracts, invoices,
-- negotiable instruments and orders for goods or services issued or made by or on behalf of the corporation.
@export Must my corporation set out its name on this document (s 10(5))?
GIVEN `the document` IS A `Kind of document under s 10(5)` @desc What kind of document is it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my corporation set out its name on this document` IF
    `the corporation must set out its name in legible characters on the document within s 10(5)` `the document`

@export Has my corporation complied with its duty to set out its name on this document (s 10(5))?
GIVEN `the document` IS A `Kind of document under s 10(5)` @desc What kind of document is it?
      `the name is in legible characters on it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation's name set out in legible characters on the document?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has my corporation complied with its duty to set out its name on this document` IF
    `the corporation has complied with the duty to set out its name within s 10(5)` (`the corporation must set out its name in legible characters on the document within s 10(5)` `the document`) `the name is in legible characters on it`

-- s 10(6). Subject to subsections 10(5) and 12(1), a corporation may carry on business under or identify
-- itself by a name other than its corporate name if that name does not contain, other than in a figurative or
-- descriptive sense, one of the corporate words or the corresponding abbreviations.
@export May my corporation carry on business under another name (s 10(6))?
GIVEN `the corporate word in the other name` IS A STRING @desc Which corporate word or abbreviation does the other name contain, other than only in a figurative or descriptive sense? (leave empty if none)
      -- out of range: the regulations (not among the sources)
      `the other name is prohibited` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the other name prohibited by the regulations, or does it fail the prescribed requirements (section 12(1))?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my corporation carry on business under another name` IF
    `the corporation may carry on business under or identify itself by the other name within s 10(6)` (LIST `the corporate word in the other name`) `the other name is prohibited`

-- s 11(1). The Director may, on request, reserve for a prescribed period a name for an intended corporation or
-- for a corporation that intends to change its name.
@export May the Director reserve a name for my intended corporation (s 11(1))?
GIVEN `I have asked the Director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you asked the Director to reserve the name?
      `the name is for an intended corporation or a name change` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the name for an intended corporation, or for a corporation that intends to change its name?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the Director reserve a name for my intended corporation` IF
    `the Director may reserve the name within s 11(1)` `I have asked the Director` `the name is for an intended corporation or a name change`

@export Until what day is my name reserved (s 11(1))?
GIVEN `the day the name was reserved` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the Director reserve the name?
      -- out of range: the regulations (not among the sources)
      `the days in the prescribed period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days is the prescribed period of reservation (it is set by the regulations)?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Until what day is my name reserved` IS
    `the last day the name stays reserved within s 11(1)` `the day the name was reserved` `the prescribed period`
    WHERE
        `the prescribed period` MEANS `Time limit` WITH
            `number of units` IS `the days in the prescribed period`
            `unit of time` IS `calendar days`

-- s 11(2). If the incorporators or the corporation ask, the Director shall assign a designating number
-- followed by "Canada" and one of the corporate words as the name.
@export Must the Director give my corporation a designating number name when we ask (s 11(2))?
GIVEN `we incorporators asked` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the incorporators asked the Director for a designating number name?
      `the corporation asked` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the corporation asked the Director for a designating number name?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the Director give my corporation a designating number name when we ask` IF
    `the Director must assign a designating number name within s 11(2)` `we incorporators asked` `the corporation asked`

@export Is my corporation's name a designating number name (s 11(2))?
GIVEN `my name is a number followed by Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the name a designating number followed by the word "Canada"?
      `the word after Canada` IS A STRING @desc What word or expression follows the word "Canada" in the name?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my corporation's name a designating number name` IF
    `the name is a designating number name within s 11(2)` `my name is a number followed by Canada` `the word after Canada`

-- s 12(1). A corporation shall not be incorporated or continued with, change its name to, or have, carry on
-- business under or identify itself by a name that is prohibited by the regulations or does not meet the
-- prescribed requirements.
@export Is my corporation's name prohibited (s 12(1))?
GIVEN
      -- out of range: the regulations (not among the sources)
      `the name is prohibited by the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the name appear on the list of names prohibited by the regulations?
      -- out of range: the regulations (not among the sources)
      `the name meets the prescribed requirements` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the name meet the requirements prescribed for names?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my corporation's name prohibited` IF
    `the name is prohibited within s 12(1)` `the name is prohibited by the regulations` `the name meets the prescribed requirements`

-- s 12(2). The Director may direct a corporation to change its name, in accordance with section 173, if it has
-- acquired a name that is prohibited or does not meet the prescribed requirements.
@export Can the Director direct my corporation to change its name (s 12(2))?
GIVEN `my corporation has acquired the name` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your corporation acquired the name it now has?
      -- out of range: the regulations (not among the sources)
      `the name is prohibited by the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the name appear on the list of names prohibited by the regulations?
      -- out of range: the regulations (not among the sources)
      `the name meets the prescribed requirements` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the name meet the requirements prescribed for names?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Director direct my corporation to change its name` IF
    `the Director may direct the corporation to change its name within s 12(2)` `my corporation has acquired the name` `the name is prohibited by the regulations` `the name meets the prescribed requirements`

-- s 12(4). If a corporation has a designating number as its name, the Director may direct it to change to a
-- name other than a designating number.
@export Can the Director direct my corporation to replace its designating number name (s 12(4))?
GIVEN `my name is a designating number` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your corporation have a designating number as its name?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Director direct my corporation to replace its designating number name` IF
    `the Director may direct the corporation to change a designating number name within s 12(4)` `my name is a designating number`

-- s 12(4.1). Where a corporation acquires its name because a person undertook to dissolve or to change names,
-- and the undertaking is not honoured, the Director may direct it to change its name unless the undertaking
-- is honoured within the period specified in subsection (5).
@export Can the Director direct my corporation to change its name because an undertaking was not honoured (s 12(4.1))?
GIVEN `I acquired the name through an undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your corporation acquire its name because a person undertook to dissolve or to change names?
      `the undertaking was honoured in time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the undertaking honoured within the period specified in subsection 12(5)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Director direct my corporation to change its name because an undertaking was not honoured` IF
    `the Director may direct the corporation to change its name because an undertaking was not honoured within s 12(4.1)` `I acquired the name through an undertaking` `the undertaking was honoured in time`

-- s 12(5). If a corporation has not followed a directive under subsection (2), (4) or (4.1) within the
-- prescribed period, the Director may revoke its name and assign a name to it.
@export Can the Director revoke my corporation's name and assign a name to it (s 12(5))?
GIVEN `the Director has directed me to change the name` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Director directed your corporation to change its name under subsection 12(2), (4) or (4.1)?
      -- out of range: the regulations (not among the sources)
      `I followed the directive in time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your corporation followed the directive within the prescribed period?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Director revoke my corporation's name and assign a name to it` IF
    `the Director may revoke the corporation's name and assign a name within s 12(5)` `the Director has directed me to change the name` `I followed the directive in time`

@export By what day must my corporation follow the Director's directive to change its name (s 12(5))?
GIVEN `the day of the directive` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the Director give the directive?
      -- out of range: the regulations (not among the sources)
      `the days in the prescribed period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days is the period for following the directive (it is set by the regulations)?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what day must my corporation follow the Director's directive` IS
    `the last day for the corporation to follow the directive within s 12(5)` `the day of the directive` `the prescribed period`
    WHERE
        `the prescribed period` MEANS `Time limit` WITH
            `number of units` IS `the days in the prescribed period`
            `unit of time` IS `calendar days`

@export What is my corporation's name now that the Director may have assigned one (s 12(5))?
GIVEN `my name before the revocation` IS A STRING @desc What was your corporation's name before any revocation?
      `the Director revoked it and assigned a name` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Director revoked the name and assigned a name?
      `the name the Director assigned` IS A STRING @desc What name did the Director assign? (leave empty if none)
      -- out of range: section 173 (piece cb4)
      `I have since changed it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you since changed the name in accordance with section 173?
      `the name I changed it to` IS A STRING @desc What name did you change it to? (leave empty if none)
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `What is my corporation's name now` IS
    `the name of the corporation within s 12(5)` `my name before the revocation` `the Director revoked it and assigned a name` `the name the Director assigned` `I have since changed it` `the name I changed it to`

-- s 13(1). When a corporation has had its name revoked and a name assigned under subsection 12(5), the
-- Director shall issue a certificate of amendment showing the new name and give public notice of it.
@export Will the Director issue a certificate of amendment and give notice after assigning my corporation a name (s 13(1))?
GIVEN `my name was revoked and another assigned` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your corporation had its name revoked and a name assigned to it under subsection 12(5)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Will the Director issue a certificate of amendment and give notice after assigning my corporation a name` IF
    `the Director must issue a certificate of amendment and give notice of the new name within s 13(1)` `my name was revoked and another assigned`

-- s 13(2). The articles are amended on the date shown in the certificate of amendment.
@export Have my corporation's articles been amended by the certificate of amendment on this day (s 13(2))?
GIVEN `the date shown in the certificate of amendment` IS A DATE @desc What date is shown in the certificate of amendment?
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you want to know whether the articles are amended?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have my corporation's articles been amended by the certificate of amendment on this day` IF
    `the articles are amended by the certificate of amendment by the day within s 13(2)` `the date shown in the certificate of amendment` `the day I am asking about`

§§ `A contract made before the corporation exists (Part II, s 14)`

-- s 14(1). A person who enters into, or purports to enter into, a written contract in the name of or on
-- behalf of a corporation before it comes into existence is personally bound by the contract and entitled to
-- its benefits, subject to s 14: the corporation's adoption of the contract (s 14(2)), a court order
-- (s 14(3)) and an express exemption in the contract (s 14(4)).
@export Am I personally bound by a contract I made for a corporation before it existed (s 14)?
GIVEN `the contract is written` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the contract in writing?
      `I entered into it for the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you enter into it, or purport to enter into it, in the name of or on behalf of the corporation?
      `the corporation did not yet exist` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had the corporation not yet come into existence when you did?
      `the corporation acted to be bound` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the corporation, by any action or conduct, signified its intention to be bound by the contract?
      `that was within a reasonable time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that within a reasonable time after the corporation came into existence?
      `the contract exempts me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the written contract expressly provide that you are not bound by it or entitled to its benefits?
      `a court has ordered that I am bound` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a court ordered, on an application under subsection 14(3), that you are bound by the contract?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I personally bound by a contract I made for a corporation before it existed` IF
    `the person is personally bound by and entitled to the benefits of the contract within s 14` `I am bound at the outset` `the corporation adopted the contract` `the contract exempts me` `a court has ordered that I am bound`
    WHERE
        `I am bound at the outset` MEANS `the person is personally bound by the pre-incorporation contract at the outset within s 14(1)` `the contract is written` `I entered into it for the corporation` `the corporation did not yet exist`
        `the corporation adopted the contract` MEANS `the corporation has adopted the contract within s 14(2)` (`the contract is written` AND `I entered into it for the corporation` AND `the corporation did not yet exist`) `the corporation acted to be bound` `that was within a reasonable time`

-- s 14(2). A corporation may, within a reasonable time after it comes into existence, by any action or
-- conduct signifying its intention to be bound, adopt a written contract made before it existed in its name
-- or on its behalf; on adoption it is bound by the contract and entitled to its benefits as if it had been a
-- party from the date of the contract.
@export Is the corporation bound by the contract it adopted (s 14(2)(a))?
GIVEN `the contract is written and was made in the corporation's name before it existed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the contract in writing, and was it made in the corporation's name or on its behalf before the corporation came into existence?
      `the corporation acted to be bound` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the corporation, by any action or conduct, signified its intention to be bound by the contract?
      `that was within a reasonable time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that within a reasonable time after the corporation came into existence?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the corporation bound by the contract it adopted` IF
    `the corporation is bound by and entitled to the benefits of the contract as if it had been a party from the date of the contract within s 14(2)(a)` (`the corporation has adopted the contract within s 14(2)` `the contract is written and was made in the corporation's name before it existed` `the corporation acted to be bound` `that was within a reasonable time`)

-- s 14(3). Whether or not the corporation adopts the contract, a party to it may apply to a court for an
-- order respecting the nature and extent of the obligations and liability of the corporation and of the person
-- who entered into it; the court may make any order it thinks fit, but not where subsection (4) exempts the
-- person.
@export May I apply to a court for an order about a contract made before the corporation existed (s 14(3))?
GIVEN `the contract is written and was made in the corporation's name before it existed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the contract in writing, and was it made in the corporation's name or on its behalf before the corporation came into existence?
      `I am a party to the contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a party to the contract?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I apply to a court for an order about a contract made before the corporation existed` IF
    `a party may apply to a court for an order within s 14(3)` `the contract is written and was made in the corporation's name before it existed` `I am a party to the contract`

@export Can a court make an order about my obligations under a contract I made for a corporation before it existed (s 14(3), (4))?
GIVEN `the contract is written and was made in the corporation's name before it existed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the contract in writing, and was it made in the corporation's name or on its behalf before the corporation came into existence?
      `a party has applied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person asking a party to the contract?
      `the contract exempts the person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the written contract expressly provide that the person who acted for the corporation is not bound by it or entitled to its benefits?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can a court make an order about my obligations under a contract I made for a corporation before it existed` IF
    `the court may make an order about the obligations of the person within s 14(3)` (`a party may apply to a court for an order within s 14(3)` `the contract is written and was made in the corporation's name before it existed` `a party has applied`) (`the person is exempt from the contract within s 14(4)` `the contract exempts the person`)

§§ `What my corporation can do, and what it cannot be said to have done (Part III, s 15 to s 18)`

-- s 15(1). A corporation has the capacity and, subject to the Act, the rights, powers and privileges of a
-- natural person. (A body that is not a corporation has none of them from this section.)
@export Does my corporation have the capacity and the rights, powers and privileges of a natural person (s 15(1))?
GIVEN `the body is a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body a corporation under the Act?
      -- out of range: the rest of this Act (pieces cb2 to cb5)
      `a provision of the Act takes it away` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a provision of the Act take the right, power or privilege away from the corporation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my corporation have the capacity and the rights, powers and privileges of a natural person` IF
    `the corporation has the right, power or privilege of a natural person within s 15(1)` `the body is a corporation` `a provision of the Act takes it away`

-- s 15(2). A corporation may carry on business throughout Canada.
@export May my corporation carry on business throughout Canada (s 15(2))?
GIVEN `the body is a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body a corporation under the Act?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my corporation carry on business throughout Canada` IF
    `the corporation may carry on business throughout Canada within s 15(2)` `the body is a corporation`

-- s 15(3). A corporation has the capacity to carry on its business, conduct its affairs and exercise its
-- powers in a jurisdiction outside Canada to the extent that the laws of that jurisdiction permit.
@export Does my corporation have the capacity to act in a jurisdiction outside Canada (s 15(3))?
GIVEN `the body is a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body a corporation under the Act?
      `the foreign law permits it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the laws of that jurisdiction permit the corporation to carry on its business, conduct its affairs and exercise its powers there?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my corporation have the capacity to act in a jurisdiction outside Canada` IF
    `the corporation has the capacity to act in the jurisdiction outside Canada within s 15(3)` `the body is a corporation` `the foreign law permits it`

-- s 16(1). It is not necessary for a by-law to be passed to confer a particular power on the corporation or
-- its directors.
@export Do the corporation or its directors have this power without a by-law (s 16(1))?
GIVEN `the power is otherwise conferred` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the power otherwise conferred on the corporation or its directors (by the Act, the articles or the law)?
      `a by-law has been passed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a by-law been passed to confer the power?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do the corporation or its directors have this power without a by-law` IF
    `the corporation or its directors have the power within s 16(1)` `the power is otherwise conferred` `a by-law has been passed`

-- s 16(2). A corporation shall not carry on any business or exercise any power it is restricted by its
-- articles from carrying on or exercising, nor exercise any power in a manner contrary to its articles.
@export Is my corporation forbidden to carry on this business or exercise this power (s 16(2))?
GIVEN `my articles restrict it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do your articles restrict the corporation from carrying on that business or exercising that power?
      `the manner is contrary to my articles` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the corporation exercise the power in a manner contrary to its articles?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my corporation forbidden to carry on this business or exercise this power` IF
    `the corporation is forbidden to carry on the business or exercise the power within s 16(2)` `my articles restrict it` `the manner is contrary to my articles`

-- s 16(3). No act of a corporation, including a transfer of property to or by it, is invalid by reason only
-- that it is contrary to its articles or to the Act.
@export Is an act of my corporation invalid (s 16(3))?
GIVEN `the act is contrary to the articles or the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the act contrary to the corporation's articles or to the Act?
      `the act is invalid on another ground` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the act invalid on some other ground (for example, fraud or illegality)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is an act of my corporation invalid` IF
    `the act of the corporation is invalid within s 16(3)` `the act is contrary to the articles or the Act` `the act is invalid on another ground`

-- s 17. No person is affected by, or deemed to have notice or knowledge of, the contents of a document
-- concerning a corporation by reason only that the Director has filed it or it is available for inspection
-- at an office of the corporation.
@export Am I affected by the contents of a document about a corporation just because it was filed (s 17)?
GIVEN `the document was filed by the Director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Director filed the document?
      `it is available for inspection at the corporation's office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it available for inspection at an office of the corporation?
      `I am otherwise affected or have notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you affected by it, or do you have notice or knowledge of its contents, for some other reason?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I affected by the contents of a document about a corporation just because it was filed` IF
    `the person is affected by or deemed to have notice of the contents of the document within s 17` `the document was filed by the Director` `it is available for inspection at the corporation's office` `I am otherwise affected or have notice`

-- s 18. A corporation, or a guarantor of its obligation, may not assert against a person dealing with the
-- corporation, or who acquired rights from it, that (a) the articles, by-laws or a unanimous shareholder
-- agreement were not complied with, (b) the persons in the latest notice under s 106 or 113 are not the
-- directors, (c) the place in the latest s 19 notice is not the registered office, (d) a person held out as a
-- director, officer or agent was not duly appointed or lacks the customary authority, (e) a document issued
-- by a director, officer or agent with actual or usual authority is not valid or genuine, or (f) a sale,
-- lease or exchange referred to in subsection 189(3) was not authorized -- except against a person who has,
-- or ought to have, knowledge of the situation through their relationship to the corporation.
@export Is the corporation barred from asserting this against me (s 18)?
GIVEN `what the corporation asserts` IS AN `Assertion barred by s 18(1)` @desc What does the corporation (or its guarantor) assert against you?
      `the one asserting is the corporation or its guarantor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the corporation, or a guarantor of an obligation of the corporation, that asserts it?
      `I dealt with the corporation or got rights from it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you deal with the corporation, or acquire rights from it?
      `I know or ought to know through my relationship to it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have, or ought you to have, knowledge of the situation by virtue of your relationship to the corporation (for example, as a director or officer)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the corporation barred from asserting this against me` IF
    `the assertion is barred against the person within s 18` `what the corporation asserts` `the one asserting is the corporation or its guarantor` `I dealt with the corporation or got rights from it` `I know or ought to know through my relationship to it`

§§ `Registered office, records and who may see them (Part IV, s 19 to s 23)`

-- s 19(1). A corporation shall at all times have a registered office in the province in Canada specified in
-- its articles.
@export Does my corporation have the registered office that the Act requires (s 19(1))?
GIVEN `it has a registered office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the corporation have a registered office?
      `it is in the province in my articles` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the registered office in the province in Canada that your articles specify?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my corporation have the registered office that the Act requires` IF
    `the corporation has the registered office that s 19(1) requires` `it has a registered office` `it is in the province in my articles`

-- s 19(2). A notice of registered office in the Director's form shall be sent to the Director together with
-- any articles that designate or change the province where the registered office is located.
@export Has my corporation sent the notice of registered office with its articles (s 19(2))?
GIVEN `my articles designate or change the province` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the articles designate or change the province where the registered office is located?
      `we sent the notice with them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a notice of registered office, in the form the Director fixes, sent to the Director together with the articles?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has my corporation sent the notice of registered office with its articles` IF
    `the corporation has complied with the duty to send a notice of registered office within s 19(2)` `my articles designate or change the province` `we sent the notice with them`

-- s 19(3). The directors may change the place and address of the registered office within the province
-- specified in the articles.
@export May the directors change the place and address of the registered office (s 19(3))?
GIVEN `the new place is within the province in my articles` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the new place and address within the province specified in the articles?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the directors change the place and address of the registered office` IF
    `the directors may change the place and address of the registered office within s 19(3)` `the new place is within the province in my articles`

-- s 19(4). A corporation shall send the Director, within fifteen days of any change of address of its
-- registered office, a notice in the Director's form, and the Director shall file it.
@export By what day must my corporation send the notice of change of address of its registered office (s 19(4))?
GIVEN `the day the address changed` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the address of the registered office change?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what day must my corporation send the notice of change of address` IS
    `the last day to send the notice of change of address within s 19(4)` `the day the address changed`

@export Did my corporation send the notice of change of address in time (s 19(4))?
GIVEN `the day the address changed` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the address of the registered office change?
      `the day we sent the notice` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the notice sent to the Director?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did my corporation send the notice of change of address in time` IF
    `the notice of change of address was sent in time within s 19(4)` `the day the address changed` `the day we sent the notice`

@export Must the Director file the notice of change of address my corporation sent (s 19(4))?
GIVEN `we sent the notice in the Director's form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you send the Director a notice of change of address in the form the Director fixes?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the Director file the notice of change of address my corporation sent` IF
    `the Director must file the notice of change of address within s 19(4)` `we sent the notice in the Director's form`

-- s 20(1). A corporation shall prepare and maintain, at its registered office or another place in Canada
-- designated by the directors, records containing (a) the articles, by-laws and amendments and a copy of any
-- unanimous shareholder agreement, (b) minutes of meetings and resolutions of shareholders, (c) copies of
-- all notices required by s 106 or 113, and (d) a securities register that complies with s 50.
@export Does my corporation keep all the records section 20(1) lists (s 20(1))?
GIVEN `we keep the articles and by-laws and agreements` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you keep the articles, the by-laws and all amendments, and a copy of any unanimous shareholder agreement?
      `we keep the shareholder minutes and resolutions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you keep minutes of meetings and resolutions of shareholders?
      -- out of range: sections 106 and 113 (piece cb2)
      `we keep copies of the director notices` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you keep copies of all notices required by section 106 or 113?
      -- out of range: section 50 (piece cb2)
      `we keep a securities register that complies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you keep a securities register that complies with section 50?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my corporation keep all the records section 20(1) lists` IF
    `the corporation keeps all the records s 20(1) lists` `our corporate records`
    WHERE
        `our corporate records` MEANS `Corporate records kept under s 20(1)` WITH
            `the articles and the by-laws, and all amendments thereto, and a copy of any unanimous shareholder agreement` IS `we keep the articles and by-laws and agreements`
            `minutes of meetings and resolutions of shareholders` IS `we keep the shareholder minutes and resolutions`
            `copies of all notices required by section 106 or 113` IS `we keep copies of the director notices`
            `a securities register that complies with section 50` IS `we keep a securities register that complies`

-- s 20(2). In addition, a corporation shall prepare and maintain adequate accounting records and records
-- containing minutes of meetings and resolutions of the directors and any committee of the directors.
@export Does my corporation keep the accounting records and directors' records section 20(2) requires (s 20(2))?
GIVEN `we keep adequate accounting records` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you keep adequate accounting records?
      `we keep the directors' and committees' minutes and resolutions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you keep records containing minutes of meetings and resolutions of the directors and any committee of the directors?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my corporation keep the accounting records and directors' records section 20(2) requires` IF
    `the corporation keeps all the records s 20(2) lists` `our directors and accounting records`
    WHERE
        `our directors and accounting records` MEANS `Directors and accounting records kept under s 20(2)` WITH
            `adequate accounting records` IS `we keep adequate accounting records`
            `records containing minutes of meetings and resolutions of the directors and any committee of the directors` IS `we keep the directors' and committees' minutes and resolutions`

-- s 20(2.1). Subject to any other federal or provincial Act that provides a longer retention period, a
-- corporation shall retain the accounting records for six years after the end of the financial year to which
-- they relate.
@export By what day must my corporation retain its accounting records (s 20(2.1))?
GIVEN `the last day of the financial year` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the financial year to which the accounting records relate?
      -- out of range: other Acts of Parliament and provincial Acts (outside the Act)
      `another Act provides a longer period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does another Act of Parliament or a provincial Act provide a longer retention period for these records?
      `the longer period in years` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, how many years? (0 if none)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what day must my corporation retain its accounting records` IS
    `the last day the corporation must retain the accounting records within s 20(2.1)` `the last day of the financial year` `the longer period`
    WHERE
        `the longer time limit` MEANS `Time limit` WITH
            `number of units` IS `the longer period in years`
            `unit of time` IS `calendar years`
        `the longer period` MEANS IF `another Act provides a longer period` THEN JUST `the longer time limit` ELSE NOTHING

-- s 20(3). Where a body corporate is continued under the Act, "records" in paragraph 20(1)(b) and subsection
-- 20(2) includes similar records required by law to be maintained by the body corporate before it was
-- continued.
@export Does a record kept before my body corporate was continued count as a record the Act requires (s 20(3))?
GIVEN `the record is one the Act lists` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the record one described in paragraph 20(1)(b) or subsection 20(2) (shareholder minutes and resolutions, accounting records, directors' minutes)?
      `my body corporate was continued under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your body corporate continued under the Act?
      `it is a similar record the law required earlier` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a similar record that the law required the body corporate to maintain before it was continued?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does a record kept before my body corporate was continued count as a record the Act requires` IF
    `the record counts as a record for paragraph 20(1)(b) and subsection 20(2) within s 20(3)` `the record is one the Act lists` `my body corporate was continued under the Act` `it is a similar record the law required earlier`

-- s 20(4). The directors' and accounting records of subsection 20(2) shall be kept at the registered office or
-- at another place the directors think fit, and shall at all reasonable times be open to inspection by the
-- directors.
@export Are my corporation's directors' and accounting records kept as the Act requires (s 20(4))?
GIVEN `the records are kept at the registered office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the records kept at the registered office?
      `the directors think fit the place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If not, have the directors decided that the place where they are kept is fit?
      `the directors can inspect them at all reasonable times` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the records open to inspection by the directors at all reasonable times?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are my corporation's directors' and accounting records kept as the Act requires` IF
    `the records of subsection 20(2) are kept as s 20(4) requires` `the records are kept at the registered office` `the directors think fit the place` `the directors can inspect them at all reasonable times`

-- s 20(5.1). Despite s 20(1) and (5), but subject to the Income Tax Act, the Excise Tax Act, the Customs Act
-- and any other Act administered by the Minister of National Revenue, a corporation may keep its corporate
-- and accounting records at a place outside Canada if they can be inspected from the registered office (or
-- another place in Canada the directors designate) by computer terminal or other technology during regular
-- office hours, and the corporation provides the technical assistance.
@export May my corporation keep its records outside Canada (s 20(5.1))?
GIVEN
      -- out of range: the Income Tax Act, the Excise Tax Act, the Customs Act and other Acts (outside the Act)
      `a tax Act requires the records to be kept in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does an Act administered by the Minister of National Revenue (such as the Income Tax Act, the Excise Tax Act or the Customs Act) require the records to be kept in Canada?
      `they can be inspected from Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the records available for inspection, by computer terminal or other technology, during regular office hours at the registered office or another place in Canada the directors designate?
      `we give the technical help` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the corporation provide the technical assistance to facilitate that inspection?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my corporation keep its records outside Canada` IF
    `the corporation may keep the records at a place outside Canada within s 20(5.1)` `a tax Act requires the records to be kept in Canada` `they can be inspected from Canada` `we give the technical help`

-- s 20(1) and (5.1). Where may the corporate records of s 20(1) be kept?
@export Are my corporation's corporate records kept at a place the Act permits (s 20(1), s 20(5.1))?
GIVEN `where we keep them` IS A `Place where corporate records are kept (Part IV)` @desc Where are the corporate records kept?
      -- out of range: the Income Tax Act, the Excise Tax Act, the Customs Act and other Acts (outside the Act)
      `a tax Act requires the records to be kept in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does an Act administered by the Minister of National Revenue require the records to be kept in Canada?
      `they can be inspected from Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the records available for inspection, by computer terminal or other technology, during regular office hours at the registered office or another place in Canada the directors designate?
      `we give the technical help` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the corporation provide the technical assistance to facilitate that inspection?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are my corporation's corporate records kept at a place the Act permits` IF
    `the corporate records are kept at a permitted place within s 20(1) and s 20(5.1)` `where we keep them` (`the corporation may keep the records at a place outside Canada within s 20(5.1)` `a tax Act requires the records to be kept in Canada` `they can be inspected from Canada` `we give the technical help`)

-- s 20(5). If accounting records are kept outside Canada, accounting records adequate to enable the directors
-- to ascertain the financial position on a quarterly basis with reasonable accuracy shall be kept at the
-- registered office or another place in Canada designated by the directors.
@export Has my corporation kept the quarterly accounting records in Canada that the Act requires (s 20(5))?
GIVEN `our accounting records are kept outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the corporation's accounting records kept outside Canada?
      -- out of range: the Income Tax Act, the Excise Tax Act, the Customs Act and other Acts (outside the Act)
      `a tax Act requires the records to be kept in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does an Act administered by the Minister of National Revenue require the records to be kept in Canada?
      `they can be inspected from Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the records available for inspection, by computer terminal or other technology, during regular office hours at the registered office or another place in Canada the directors designate?
      `we give the technical help` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the corporation provide the technical assistance to facilitate that inspection?
      `we keep quarterly records in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are accounting records adequate to ascertain the corporation's financial position with reasonable accuracy on a quarterly basis kept at the registered office or another place in Canada the directors designate?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has my corporation kept the quarterly accounting records in Canada that the Act requires` IF
    `the corporation has complied with the duty to keep quarterly accounting records in Canada within s 20(5)` `our accounting records are kept outside Canada` (`the corporation may keep the records at a place outside Canada within s 20(5.1)` `a tax Act requires the records to be kept in Canada` `they can be inspected from Canada` `we give the technical help`) `we keep quarterly records in Canada`

-- s 20(6). A corporation that, without reasonable cause, fails to comply with section 20 is guilty of an
-- offence and liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding five thousand dollars.
@export Is my corporation guilty of an offence for failing to comply with the records section (s 20(6))?
GIVEN `we failed to comply with section 20` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the corporation failed to comply with section 20?
      `we had reasonable cause` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the corporation have reasonable cause for failing to comply?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my corporation guilty of an offence for failing to comply with the records section` IF
    `the corporation is guilty of an offence within s 20(6)` `we failed to comply with section 20` `we had reasonable cause`

-- s 21(1) and (1.1). Shareholders and creditors, their personal representatives and the Director may examine
-- the s 20(1) records during usual business hours and take extracts free of charge; if the corporation is a
-- distributing corporation, any other person may do so on payment of a reasonable fee. To examine the
-- securities register of a distributing corporation a request with an affidavit (s 21(7)) must come first.
@export What access do I have to the corporation's records (s 21(1), (1.1))?
GIVEN `who I am` IS A `Person seeking to examine the corporate records (s 21)` @desc Who are you in relation to the corporation?
      -- out of range: section 2(1) (keel)
      `it is a distributing corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation a distributing corporation?
      `I want to see the securities register` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you want to examine the securities register?
      `I made a request with the affidavit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you made a request to the corporation or its agent, accompanied by the affidavit that subsection 21(7) describes?
GIVETH AN `Access to the corporate records under s 21(1) and s 21(1.1)`
DECIDE `What access do I have to the corporation's records` IS
    `the access the person has to the corporate records within s 21(1) and s 21(1.1)` `who I am` `it is a distributing corporation` `I want to see the securities register` `I made a request with the affidavit`

-- s 21(2). A shareholder is entitled on request and without charge to one copy of the articles and by-laws and
-- of any unanimous shareholder agreement.
@export Am I entitled to a free copy of the articles, by-laws and any unanimous shareholder agreement (s 21(2))?
GIVEN `I am a shareholder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a shareholder of the corporation?
      `I have asked for a copy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you asked the corporation for a copy?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I entitled to a free copy of the articles by-laws and any unanimous shareholder agreement` IF
    `the shareholder is entitled to one copy of the articles, by-laws and any unanimous shareholder agreement, without charge, within s 21(2)` `I am a shareholder` `I have asked for a copy`

-- s 21(3). On payment of a reasonable fee and on sending the affidavit (s 21(7)), shareholders and creditors,
-- their personal representatives, the Director and, for a distributing corporation, any other person may
-- require the corporation to provide a "basic list" of shareholders within 10 days after the receipt of the
-- affidavit, made up to a date not more than 10 days before the date of receipt.
@export May I require the corporation to give me a list of its shareholders (s 21(3))?
GIVEN `who I am` IS A `Person seeking to examine the corporate records (s 21)` @desc Who are you in relation to the corporation?
      -- out of range: section 2(1) (keel)
      `it is a distributing corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation a distributing corporation?
      `I have paid a reasonable fee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you paid a reasonable fee?
      `I sent the affidavit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you sent the corporation or its agent the affidavit that subsection 21(7) describes?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I require the corporation to give me a list of its shareholders` IF
    `the person may require the corporation to provide a basic list within s 21(3)` `who I am` `it is a distributing corporation` `I have paid a reasonable fee` `I sent the affidavit`

@export By what day must the corporation give me the list of shareholders (s 21(3))?
GIVEN `the day the corporation received the affidavit` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the corporation (or its agent) receive your affidavit?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what day must the corporation give me the list of shareholders` IS
    `the last day to provide the basic list within s 21(3)` `the day the corporation received the affidavit`

@export What is the earliest date the list of shareholders may be made up to (s 21(3))?
GIVEN `the day the corporation received the affidavit` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the corporation (or its agent) receive your affidavit?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `What is the earliest date the list of shareholders may be made up to` IS
    `the earliest date the basic list may be made up to within s 21(3)` `the day the corporation received the affidavit`

@export Has the corporation given me the list of shareholders as the Act requires (s 21(3))?
GIVEN `the day the corporation received the affidavit` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the corporation (or its agent) receive your affidavit?
      `the day I got the list` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the list provided to you?
      `the date the list is made up to` IS A DATE @desc To what date is the list made up?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has the corporation given me the list of shareholders as the Act requires` IF
    `the corporation has provided the basic list as s 21(3) requires` `the day the corporation received the affidavit` `the day I got the list` `the date the list is made up to`

-- s 21(4). A person requiring a basic list may, by stating in the affidavit that they require supplemental
-- lists, require the corporation on payment of a reasonable fee to provide supplemental lists of changes for
-- each business day following the date the basic list is made up to.
@export May I require supplemental lists of changes in the shareholders (s 21(4))?
GIVEN `I required a basic list` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you required a basic list under subsection 21(3)?
      `my affidavit says I need supplemental lists` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your affidavit state that you require supplemental lists?
      `I have paid a reasonable fee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you paid a reasonable fee?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I require supplemental lists of changes in the shareholders` IF
    `the person may require supplemental lists within s 21(4)` `I required a basic list` `my affidavit says I need supplemental lists` `I have paid a reasonable fee`

-- s 21(5). The corporation shall provide a supplemental list (a) on the date the basic list is furnished,
-- where the information relates to changes before that date, and (b) on the business day following the day to
-- which the list relates, where it relates to changes on or after that date. ("Business day" is not defined
-- in the Act; the day is therefore asked.)
@export On what day is a supplemental list due to me (s 21(5))?
GIVEN `the date the basic list is furnished` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the basic list furnished to you?
      `the day the supplemental list relates to` IS A DATE @desc To what day do the changes in the supplemental list relate?
      -- out of range: "business day" is not defined in the text (not in the sources)
      `the business day after that day` IS A DATE @desc What is the business day following the day to which the supplemental list relates?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `On what day is a supplemental list due to me` IS
    `the day the supplemental list is due within s 21(5)` `the date the basic list is furnished` `the day the supplemental list relates to` `the business day after that day`

-- s 21(6). A person requiring a basic or a supplemental list may also require the corporation to include the
-- name and address of any known holder of an option or right to acquire shares.
@export May I also require the list to include holders of options or rights to acquire shares (s 21(6))?
GIVEN `I require a basic or supplemental list` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you requiring a basic list or a supplemental list?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I also require the list to include holders of options or rights to acquire shares` IF
    `the person may also require the list to include the known holders of options within s 21(6)` `I require a basic or supplemental list`

-- s 21(7) and (8). The affidavit shall state the name and address of the applicant; if the applicant is a
-- body corporate, its name and address for service; and that the lists or register information will not be used
-- except as permitted by subsection (9). If the applicant is a body corporate, the affidavit shall be made by a
-- director or officer of it.
@export Does my affidavit say what the Act requires (s 21(7), (8))?
GIVEN `my affidavit states my name and address` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the affidavit state the name and address of the applicant?
      `the applicant is a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the applicant a body corporate?
      `my affidavit states the address for service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, does the affidavit state the name and address for service of the body corporate?
      `my affidavit promises limited use` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the affidavit state that the lists or the securities register information will not be used except as subsection 21(9) permits?
      `a director or officer made the affidavit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the applicant is a body corporate, was the affidavit made by a director or officer of it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my affidavit say what the Act requires` IF
    `the affidavit has the contents s 21(7) and s 21(8) require` `my affidavit`
    WHERE
        `my affidavit` MEANS `Affidavit under s 21(7)` WITH
            `states the name and address of the applicant` IS `my affidavit states my name and address`
            `the applicant is a body corporate` IS `the applicant is a body corporate`
            `states the name and address for service of the body corporate` IS `my affidavit states the address for service`
            `states that the lists or the securities register information will not be used except as permitted under subsection 21(9)` IS `my affidavit promises limited use`
            `is made by a director or officer of the body corporate` IS `a director or officer made the affidavit`

-- s 21(9). A list of shareholders or information from a securities register obtained under s 21 shall not be
-- used except in connection with an effort to influence the voting of shareholders, an offer to acquire
-- securities of the corporation, or any other matter relating to the affairs of the corporation.
@export May I use the shareholder list or register information I obtained for this purpose (s 21(9))?
GIVEN `what I want to use it for` IS A `Use of a shareholder list or securities register information (s 21(9))` @desc What do you want to use the list or information for?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I use the shareholder list or register information I obtained for this purpose` IF
    `the use of the list or information is permitted within s 21(9)` `what I want to use it for`

-- s 21(10). A person who, without reasonable cause, contravenes section 21 is guilty of an offence and liable
-- on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding five thousand dollars or to imprisonment for a term not
-- exceeding six months or both.
@export Am I guilty of an offence for contravening the access section (s 21(10))?
GIVEN `I contravened section 21` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you contravened section 21 (for example, by using a list for a purpose that subsection 21(9) does not permit)?
      `I had reasonable cause` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have reasonable cause?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I guilty of an offence for contravening the access section` IF
    `the person is guilty of an offence within s 21(10)` `I contravened section 21` `I had reasonable cause`

§§ `Individuals with significant control (Part IV, s 21.1 to s 21.4)`

-- This group applies only to a corporation to which section 21.1 applies (not a reporting issuer, not listed
-- on a designated stock exchange, not in a prescribed class): the form may ask "Is your corporation one that
-- must keep a register of individuals with significant control?" before showing it. Section 21.32 binds an
-- investigative body, not this seat, and has no question here; it is encoded in cb1-part4-isc-register.l4.

-- s 21.1(7). Section 21.1 does not apply to a corporation that is a reporting issuer, whose securities are
-- listed and posted for trading on a designated stock exchange, or that is a member of a prescribed class.
@export Must my corporation keep a register of individuals with significant control (s 21.1(7))?
GIVEN
      -- out of range: provincial securities Acts (outside the Act)
      `it is a reporting issuer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation a reporting issuer (or an émetteur assujetti) under a provincial securities Act?
      -- out of range: section 248(1) of the Income Tax Act (outside the Act)
      `its securities are listed on a designated stock exchange` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are any of its securities listed and posted for trading on a designated stock exchange, as defined in subsection 248(1) of the Income Tax Act?
      -- out of range: the regulations (not among the sources)
      `it is in a prescribed class` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a member of a class of corporations prescribed by the regulations?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my corporation keep a register of individuals with significant control` IF
    `section 21.1 applies to the corporation within s 21.1(7)` `it is a reporting issuer` `its securities are listed on a designated stock exchange` `it is in a prescribed class`

-- s 21.1(1). The register is kept at the registered office or another place in Canada designated by the
-- directors, and contains, for each individual with significant control, their name and date of birth,
-- residential address and address for service (if provided), citizenship, jurisdiction of residence for tax
-- purposes, the day they became or ceased to be one, a description of how they are one, any other prescribed
-- information, and a description of each step taken under s 21.1(2).
@export Does my corporation's register of individuals with significant control contain what the Act requires (s 21.1(1))?
GIVEN `the register is kept where the Act allows` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the register kept at the registered office or at another place in Canada designated by the directors?
      `it has each name and date of birth` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it contain the name and date of birth of each individual with significant control?
      `it has each residential address` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it contain the residential address of each individual with significant control?
      `an address for service has been provided` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an address for service been provided to the corporation?
      `it has each address for service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the register contain the address for service of each individual with significant control?
      `it has each citizenship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it contain the citizenship of each individual with significant control?
      `it has each tax residence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it contain the jurisdiction of residence for tax purposes of each individual with significant control?
      `it has each day they began or ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it contain the day on which each individual became or ceased to be an individual with significant control?
      `it describes how each has significant control` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it describe how each individual is an individual with significant control, including their interests and rights in respect of shares?
      -- out of range: the regulations (not among the sources)
      `other information is prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the regulations prescribe other information for the register?
      -- out of range: the regulations (not among the sources)
      `it has the other prescribed information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, does the register contain it?
      `it describes each step taken` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it describe each step taken to update it under subsection 21.1(2)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my corporation's register of individuals with significant control contain what the Act requires` IF
    `the register contains what s 21.1(1) requires` `our register`
    WHERE
        `our register` MEANS `Register of individuals with significant control as kept (s 21.1(1))` WITH
            `the register is kept at the registered office or at another place in Canada designated by the directors` IS `the register is kept where the Act allows`
            `it contains the name and date of birth of each individual with significant control` IS `it has each name and date of birth`
            `it contains the residential address of each individual with significant control` IS `it has each residential address`
            `an address for service has been provided to the corporation` IS `an address for service has been provided`
            `it contains the address for service of each individual with significant control` IS `it has each address for service`
            `it contains the citizenship of each individual with significant control` IS `it has each citizenship`
            `it contains the jurisdiction of residence for tax purposes of each individual with significant control` IS `it has each tax residence`
            `it contains the day on which each individual became or ceased to be an individual with significant control` IS `it has each day they began or ended`
            `it contains a description of how each individual is an individual with significant control over the corporation, including a description of their interests and rights in respect of shares` IS `it describes how each has significant control`
            `there is other prescribed information` IS `other information is prescribed`
            `it contains the other prescribed information` IS `it has the other prescribed information`
            `it contains a description of each step taken in accordance with subsection 21.1(2)` IS `it describes each step taken`

-- s 21.1(2). The corporation shall, at least once each financial year, on the Director's request and at the
-- times the regulations provide, take reasonable steps to identify all individuals with significant control and
-- to ensure the register is accurate, complete and up to date.
@export Has my corporation taken the steps the Act requires to keep its register up to date (s 21.1(2))?
GIVEN `we took reasonable steps this financial year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the corporation take reasonable steps during the financial year to identify all individuals with significant control and to ensure that the register is accurate, complete and up to date?
      `the Director asked for the steps` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Director requested that the steps be taken?
      `we took them on the Director's request` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the corporation take the steps on that request?
      -- out of range: the regulations (not among the sources)
      `the regulations fix a time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the regulations provide for a time at which the steps must be taken?
      `we took them at that time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the corporation take the steps at that time?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has my corporation taken the steps the Act requires to keep its register up to date` IF
    `the corporation has taken the steps s 21.1(2) requires` `we took reasonable steps this financial year` `the Director asked for the steps` `we took them on the Director's request` `the regulations fix a time` `we took them at that time`

-- s 21.1(3). If the corporation becomes aware of information that the register must contain, it shall record
-- it in the register within 15 days of becoming aware of it.
@export By what day must my corporation record new information in the register (s 21.1(3))?
GIVEN `the day we became aware` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the corporation become aware of the information?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what day must my corporation record new information in the register` IS
    `the last day to record the information in the register within s 21.1(3)` `the day we became aware`

@export Did my corporation record the information in the register in time (s 21.1(3))?
GIVEN `the day we became aware` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the corporation become aware of the information?
      `the day we recorded it` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the corporation record the information in the register?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did my corporation record the information in the register in time` IF
    `the corporation recorded the information in time within s 21.1(3)` `the day we became aware` `the day we recorded it`

-- s 21.1(4). If the corporation requests the register information from a shareholder, the shareholder shall,
-- to the best of their knowledge, reply accurately and completely as soon as feasible.
@export Have I, as a shareholder, complied with the duty to answer the corporation's request for register information (s 21.1(4))?
GIVEN `the corporation asked me for the information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the corporation requested from you any information the register must contain (names, addresses, dates, how a person has significant control)?
      `I replied accurately and completely` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you reply accurately and completely, to the best of your knowledge?
      `I replied as soon as feasible` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you reply as soon as feasible?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I as a shareholder complied with the duty to answer the corporation's request for register information` IF
    `the shareholder has complied with the duty to reply within s 21.1(4)` `the corporation asked me for the information` `I replied accurately and completely` `I replied as soon as feasible`

-- s 21.1(5). Within one year after the sixth anniversary of the day an individual ceases to be an individual
-- with significant control, the corporation shall -- subject to any longer retention period under another
-- Act -- dispose of that individual's personal information recorded in the register.
@export By what day must the corporation dispose of my personal information in the register (s 21.1(5))?
GIVEN `I have ceased to have significant control` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you ceased to be an individual with significant control over the corporation?
      `the day I ceased` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you cease? (any date if you have not)
      -- out of range: other Acts of Parliament and provincial Acts (outside the Act)
      `another Act provides a longer retention period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does another Act of Parliament or a provincial Act provide a longer retention period?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `By what day must the corporation dispose of my personal information in the register` IS
    `the last day to dispose of the personal information within s 21.1(5)` `the day I ceased if I have` `another Act provides a longer retention period`
    WHERE
        `the day I ceased if I have` MEANS IF `I have ceased to have significant control` THEN JUST `the day I ceased` ELSE NOTHING

-- s 21.1(6). A corporation that, without reasonable cause, contravenes section 21.1 is guilty of an offence
-- and liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding $100,000.
@export Is my corporation guilty of an offence for contravening the register section (s 21.1(6))?
GIVEN `we contravened section 21.1` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the corporation contravened section 21.1?
      `we had reasonable cause` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the corporation have reasonable cause?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my corporation guilty of an offence for contravening the register section` IF
    `the corporation is guilty of an offence within s 21.1(6)` `we contravened section 21.1` `we had reasonable cause`

-- s 21.2. A corporation to which section 21.1 applies shall take prescribed steps if it is unable to identify
-- any individuals with significant control over it.
@export Has my corporation taken the prescribed steps when it cannot identify anyone with significant control (s 21.2)?
GIVEN `section 21.1 applies to us` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 21.1 apply to the corporation?
      `we cannot identify any individual with significant control` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation unable to identify any individuals with significant control over it?
      -- out of range: the regulations (not among the sources)
      `we took the prescribed steps` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the corporation taken the steps the regulations prescribe?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has my corporation taken the prescribed steps when it cannot identify anyone with significant control` IF
    `the corporation has complied with the duty to take prescribed steps within s 21.2` `section 21.1 applies to us` `we cannot identify any individual with significant control` `we took the prescribed steps`

-- s 21.21(1)(a). A corporation to which section 21.1 applies shall send the Director, annually, the
-- information the Director determines from its register, in the form and within the period the Director fixes.
@export Has my corporation sent the Director its annual information from the register (s 21.21(1)(a))?
GIVEN `section 21.1 applies to us` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 21.1 apply to the corporation?
      `we sent the annual information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the corporation send the Director, on an annual basis, the information the Director determined, in the form and within the period the Director fixes?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has my corporation sent the Director its annual information from the register` IF
    `the corporation has sent the annual information within s 21.21(1)(a)` `section 21.1 applies to us` `we sent the annual information`

-- s 21.21(1)(b). The information recorded under s 21.1(3) that the Director determines shall be sent within 15
-- days after it is recorded, in the form the Director fixes.
@export By what day must my corporation send the newly recorded information to the Director (s 21.21(1)(b))?
GIVEN `the day we recorded the information` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the information recorded under subsection 21.1(3)?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what day must my corporation send the newly recorded information to the Director` IS
    `the last day to send the recorded information to the Director within s 21.21(1)(b)` `the day we recorded the information`

@export Did my corporation send the newly recorded information to the Director in time (s 21.21(1)(b))?
GIVEN `section 21.1 applies to us` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 21.1 apply to the corporation?
      `the day we recorded the information` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the information recorded under subsection 21.1(3)?
      `the day we sent it` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the corporation send the information to the Director?
      `we sent it in the Director's form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it sent in the form the Director fixes?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did my corporation send the newly recorded information to the Director in time` IF
    `the corporation has sent the recorded information in time within s 21.21(1)(b)` `section 21.1 applies to us` `the day we recorded the information` `the day we sent it` `we sent it in the Director's form`

-- s 21.21(2). On or after the date shown on a certificate referred to in section 8 or subsection 185(4) or
-- 187(4), a corporation to which section 21.1 applies shall send the Director the information determined by
-- the Director, in the form and within the period the Director fixes.
@export Has my corporation complied with its duty to send register information on a new certificate (s 21.21(2))?
GIVEN `section 21.1 applies to us` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 21.1 apply to the corporation?
      -- out of range: sections 185(4) and 187(4) (piece cb4)
      `the date on our certificate` IS A DATE @desc What date is shown on the certificate (of incorporation under section 8, or of amalgamation or continuance under subsection 185(4) or 187(4))?
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you want to know whether the duty has arisen?
      `we sent the information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the corporation send the Director the information the Director determined, in the form and within the period the Director fixes?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has my corporation complied with its duty to send register information on a new certificate` IF
    `the corporation has complied with the duty to send information on a certificate within s 21.21(2)` (`the duty to send information to the Director has arisen within s 21.21(2)` `section 21.1 applies to us` `the date on our certificate` `the day I am asking about`) `we sent the information`

-- s 21.21(4). A corporation that, without reasonable cause, contravenes subsection 21.21(1) or (2) is guilty
-- of an offence and liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding $100,000.
@export Is my corporation guilty of an offence for not sending register information to the Director (s 21.21(4))?
GIVEN `we contravened subsection 21.21(1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the corporation contravened subsection 21.21(1) or (2)?
      `we had reasonable cause` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the corporation have reasonable cause?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my corporation guilty of an offence for not sending register information to the Director` IF
    `the corporation is guilty of an offence within s 21.21(4)` `we contravened subsection 21.21(1) or (2)` `we had reasonable cause`

-- s 21.3(1). A corporation to which section 21.1 applies shall disclose to the Director, on request, any
-- information in its register.
@export Must my corporation disclose the information in its register to the Director when asked (s 21.3(1))?
GIVEN `section 21.1 applies to us` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 21.1 apply to the corporation?
      `the Director has asked` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Director requested the disclosure?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my corporation disclose the information in its register to the Director when asked` IF
    `the corporation must disclose the information in its register to the Director within s 21.3(1)` `section 21.1 applies to us` `the Director has asked`

-- s 21.301 and s 21.302. The Director may provide the information received under s 21.21 to an investigative
-- body, the Financial Transactions and Reports Analysis Centre of Canada or a prescribed entity (s 21.301),
-- and to a provincial corporate registry or a provincial department or agency responsible for corporate law
-- (s 21.302).
@export Can the Director pass on the information my corporation sent about me to this recipient (s 21.301, s 21.302)?
GIVEN `the recipient` IS A `Recipient of information from the Director (s 21.301, s 21.302)` @desc Who would receive the information?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Director pass on the information my corporation sent about me to this recipient` IF
    `the Director may provide the information received under section 21.21 to the recipient within s 21.301 and s 21.302` `the recipient`

-- s 21.303(1), (2). The Director shall make available to the public, for each individual with significant
-- control, their name; their address for service if provided to the corporation; their residential address if
-- no address for service was provided; the information in paragraphs 21.1(1)(c) and (d); and any other
-- prescribed information -- but not for an individual under 18 or one to whom prescribed circumstances apply
-- (subsection (2)), and not where the Director has chosen under subsection (3) not to.
@export Must the Director make this information about me available to the public (s 21.303)?
GIVEN `the item` IS AN `Item of information about an individual with significant control (s 21.303(1))` @desc Which item of information about you is in question?
      `an address for service was provided to the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your address for service been provided to the corporation?
      `I am under 18` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you less than 18 years of age?
      -- out of range: the regulations (not among the sources)
      `prescribed circumstances apply to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do circumstances prescribed by the regulations apply to you?
      `the Director has chosen not to publish it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Director chosen, on your application or the corporation's, not to make the information available to the public?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the Director make this information about me available to the public` IF
    `the Director must make the item available to the public within s 21.303` `the item` `an address for service was provided to the corporation` `I am under 18` `prescribed circumstances apply to me` `the Director has chosen not to publish it`

-- s 21.303(3). If an individual with significant control or the corporation applies, the Director may choose
-- not to make information about the individual available to the public, subject to terms, if the Director
-- reasonably believes it presents a serious threat to the individual's safety, or is satisfied that the
-- individual is incapable, that the information is to be kept confidential under subsection 27(8) of the
-- Conflict of Interest Act or a similar provincial provision, or that prescribed circumstances apply.
@export Can the Director choose not to make my information public if I apply (s 21.303(3))?
GIVEN `I or the corporation applied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you, or the corporation over which you have significant control, applied to the Director to have the information not made available to the public?
      `the Director believes it threatens my safety` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Director reasonably believe that making it available presents or would present a serious threat to your safety?
      `the Director is satisfied I am incapable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Director satisfied that you are incapable?
      -- out of range: section 27(8) of the Conflict of Interest Act (outside the Act)
      `the Director is satisfied it is confidential` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Director satisfied that the information is to be kept confidential under subsection 27(8) of the Conflict of Interest Act or a similar provincial provision?
      -- out of range: the regulations (not among the sources)
      `the Director is satisfied prescribed circumstances apply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Director satisfied that prescribed circumstances apply to you?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Director choose not to make my information public if I apply` IF
    `the Director may choose not to make the information available to the public within s 21.303(3)` `I or the corporation applied` `the Director believes it threatens my safety` `the Director is satisfied I am incapable` `the Director is satisfied it is confidential` `the Director is satisfied prescribed circumstances apply`

-- s 21.31(1) and (2). On request by an investigative body (a police force, the Canada Revenue Agency or a
-- similar provincial body, or a prescribed body), a corporation to which section 21.1 applies shall, as soon as
-- feasible after the request is served or deemed received, provide a copy of the register or disclose
-- specified information from it.
@export Must my corporation give this body a copy of its register or the information it asks for (s 21.31(1))?
GIVEN `the body that asked` IS AN `Investigative body (s 21.31(2))` @desc What kind of body made the request?
      `section 21.1 applies to us` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 21.1 apply to the corporation?
      `the request was served or is deemed received` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the request been served on the corporation, or is it deemed to have been received by it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my corporation give this body a copy of its register or the information it asks for` IF
    `the corporation must provide the copy of its register or disclose the specified information within s 21.31(1)` `the body that asked` `section 21.1 applies to us` `the request was served or is deemed received`

@export Is the body that asked for my corporation's register an investigative body (s 21.31(2))?
GIVEN `the body that asked` IS AN `Investigative body (s 21.31(2))` @desc What kind of body made the request?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the body that asked for my corporation's register an investigative body` IF
    `the body is an investigative body for the purpose of s 21.31 within s 21.31(2)` `the body that asked`

-- s 21.31(3). An investigative body may make a request only if it has reasonable grounds to suspect that the
-- copy or information would be relevant to investigating an offence in the schedule and also has reasonable
-- grounds to suspect that (a) the corporation committed the offence or was used to commit or facilitate it or
-- to protect an offender, (b) an individual with significant control is also one over a corporation that did,
-- or (c) such an individual influences the affairs of a non-corporate entity that did.
@export Has the investigative body made a request it was entitled to make (s 21.31(3))?
GIVEN `the body suspects the register is relevant to a scheduled offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the body have reasonable grounds to suspect that the register or information would be relevant to investigating an offence referred to in the schedule?
      `the body suspects our corporation was involved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it have reasonable grounds to suspect that your corporation committed the offence or was used to commit it, to facilitate it or to protect from detection or punishment a person who committed it?
      `the body suspects a controller of ours controls an involved corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it have reasonable grounds to suspect that an individual with significant control over your corporation also has significant control over a corporation that did any of those things?
      `the body suspects a controller of ours influences an involved entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it have reasonable grounds to suspect that an individual with significant control over your corporation also directly or indirectly influences the affairs of an entity other than a corporation that did any of those things?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has the investigative body made a request it was entitled to make` IF
    `the investigative body may make the request within s 21.31(3)` `the body suspects the register is relevant to a scheduled offence` `the body suspects our corporation was involved` `the body suspects a controller of ours controls an involved corporation` `the body suspects a controller of ours influences an involved entity`

-- s 21.31(4). The request must be served by leaving it at the registered office shown in the last notice filed
-- under s 19, or sent by registered mail to that office; if mailed, it is deemed received when it would be
-- delivered in the ordinary course of mail, unless there are reasonable grounds for believing the corporation
-- did not receive it then or at all.
@export On what day is the request served or deemed received (s 21.31(4))?
GIVEN `it was left at our registered office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the request left at the corporation's registered office?
      `the day it was left` IS A DATE @desc On what day was it left? (any date if it was not)
      `it was sent by registered mail` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the request sent by registered mail to the registered office?
      `the day it would be delivered in the ordinary course` IS A DATE @desc On what day would it be delivered in the ordinary course of mail? (any date if it was not mailed)
      `there are grounds to believe we did not receive it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are there reasonable grounds for believing that the corporation did not receive the request at that time or at all?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `On what day is the request served or deemed received` IS
    `the day the request is served or deemed received within s 21.31(4)` `the day left if it was` `the day mailed delivery if it was mailed` `there are grounds to believe we did not receive it`
    WHERE
        `the day left if it was` MEANS IF `it was left at our registered office` THEN JUST `the day it was left` ELSE NOTHING
        `the day mailed delivery if it was mailed` MEANS IF `it was sent by registered mail` THEN JUST `the day it would be delivered in the ordinary course` ELSE NOTHING

-- s 21.31(5). A corporation that, without reasonable cause, contravenes subsection 21.31(1) is guilty of an
-- offence and liable on summary conviction to a fine of not more than $100,000.
@export Is my corporation guilty of an offence for not answering an investigative body's request (s 21.31(5))?
GIVEN `we contravened subsection 21.31(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the corporation contravened subsection 21.31(1)?
      `we had reasonable cause` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the corporation have reasonable cause?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my corporation guilty of an offence for not answering an investigative body's request` IF
    `the corporation is guilty of an offence within s 21.31(5)` `we contravened subsection 21.31(1)` `we had reasonable cause`

-- s 21.4(1). A director or officer who knowingly authorizes, permits or acquiesces in the corporation's
-- contravention of s 21.1(1), 21.21(1) or (2), 21.3(1) or 21.31(1) commits an offence, whether or not the
-- corporation has been prosecuted or convicted.
@export Do I commit an offence as a director or officer by allowing the corporation to contravene the register provisions (s 21.4(1))?
GIVEN `I am a director or officer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director or officer of the corporation?
      `the corporation contravened one of those provisions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the corporation contravene subsection 21.1(1), 21.21(1) or (2), 21.3(1) or 21.31(1)?
      `I knowingly authorized, permitted or acquiesced` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you knowingly authorize, permit or acquiesce in the contravention?
      `the corporation has been prosecuted or convicted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the corporation been prosecuted or convicted?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I commit an offence as a director or officer by allowing the corporation to contravene the register provisions` IF
    `the director or officer commits an offence within s 21.4(1)` `I am a director or officer` `the corporation contravened one of those provisions` `I knowingly authorized, permitted or acquiesced` `the corporation has been prosecuted or convicted`

-- s 21.4(2). A director or officer who knowingly records, or knowingly authorizes, permits or acquiesces in
-- the recording of, false or misleading information in the register commits an offence.
@export Do I commit an offence as a director or officer by recording false or misleading information in the register (s 21.4(2))?
GIVEN `I am a director or officer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director or officer of the corporation?
      `I knowingly recorded or allowed false information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you knowingly record, or knowingly authorize, permit or acquiesce in the recording of, false or misleading information in the register?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I commit an offence as a director or officer by recording false or misleading information in the register` IF
    `the director or officer commits an offence within s 21.4(2)` `I am a director or officer` `I knowingly recorded or allowed false information`

-- s 21.4(3). A director or officer who knowingly provides, or knowingly authorizes, permits or acquiesces in
-- the provision to any person or entity of, false or misleading information in relation to the register commits
-- an offence.
@export Do I commit an offence as a director or officer by giving anyone false or misleading information about the register (s 21.4(3))?
GIVEN `I am a director or officer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director or officer of the corporation?
      `I knowingly gave or allowed giving false information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you knowingly provide, or knowingly authorize, permit or acquiesce in the provision to any person or entity of, false or misleading information in relation to the register?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I commit an offence as a director or officer by giving anyone false or misleading information about the register` IF
    `the director or officer commits an offence within s 21.4(3)` `I am a director or officer` `I knowingly gave or allowed giving false information`

-- s 21.4(4). A shareholder who knowingly contravenes subsection 21.1(4) commits an offence.
@export Do I commit an offence as a shareholder by knowingly not answering the corporation's request for register information (s 21.4(4))?
GIVEN `I am a shareholder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a shareholder of the corporation?
      `I knowingly contravened subsection 21.1(4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you knowingly contravene subsection 21.1(4) (the duty to reply accurately, completely and as soon as feasible)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I commit an offence as a shareholder by knowingly not answering the corporation's request for register information` IF
    `the shareholder commits an offence within s 21.4(4)` `I am a shareholder` `I knowingly contravened subsection 21.1(4)`

-- s 21.4(5). A person who commits an offence under s 21.4(1) to (4) is liable on summary conviction to a fine
-- not exceeding $200,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding two years, or both, or on conviction on
-- indictment to a fine not exceeding $1,000,000 or imprisonment not exceeding five years, or both.
@export What is the most I can be fined for an offence under section 21.4, in dollars (s 21.4(5))?
GIVEN `how I am prosecuted` IS A `Mode of prosecution (s 21.4(5))` @desc Is the offence prosecuted by summary conviction or by indictment?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most I can be fined for an offence under section 21.4` IS
    (`the most a court may impose within s 21.4(5)` `how I am prosecuted`)'s `maximum fine in dollars`

@export What is the longest term of imprisonment I can receive for an offence under section 21.4, in months (s 21.4(5))?
GIVEN `how I am prosecuted` IS A `Mode of prosecution (s 21.4(5))` @desc Is the offence prosecuted by summary conviction or by indictment?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the longest term of imprisonment I can receive for an offence under section 21.4` IS
    (`the most a court may impose within s 21.4(5)` `how I am prosecuted`)'s `maximum imprisonment in months`

§§ `Form of records, and the corporate seal (Part IV, s 22 and s 23)`

-- s 22(1). A register or other record may be in a bound or loose-leaf form, a photographic film form, or be
-- entered or recorded by a system of mechanical or electronic data processing or any other information
-- storage device, if the system is capable of reproducing the information in intelligible written form
-- within a reasonable time.
@export May my corporation keep its registers and records in this form (s 22(1))?
GIVEN `the form` IS A `Form of a register or other record (s 22(1))` @desc In what form does the corporation keep the register or record?
      `it can reproduce the information in writing in a reasonable time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the system or device capable of reproducing any required information in intelligible written form within a reasonable time?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my corporation keep its registers and records in this form` IF
    `the form of the record is permitted within s 22(1)` `the form` `it can reproduce the information in writing in a reasonable time`

-- s 22(2). The corporation and its agents shall take reasonable precautions to prevent loss or destruction
-- of, and falsification of entries in, the registers and other records, and to facilitate detection and
-- correction of inaccuracies.
@export Has my corporation taken the precautions the Act requires for its registers and records (s 22(2))?
GIVEN `we guard against loss or destruction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the corporation and its agents taken reasonable precautions to prevent loss or destruction of the registers and other records?
      `we guard against falsification` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have they taken reasonable precautions to prevent falsification of entries?
      `we can detect and correct inaccuracies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have they taken reasonable precautions to facilitate detection and correction of inaccuracies?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has my corporation taken the precautions the Act requires for its registers and records` IF
    `the corporation or its agents or mandataries have taken the precautions s 22(2) requires` `we guard against loss or destruction` `we guard against falsification` `we can detect and correct inaccuracies`

-- s 22(3). A person who, without reasonable cause, contravenes section 22 is guilty of an offence.
@export Am I guilty of an offence for contravening the form and precautions section (s 22(3))?
GIVEN `I contravened section 22` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you contravened section 22?
      `I had reasonable cause` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have reasonable cause?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I guilty of an offence for contravening the form and precautions section` IF
    `the person is guilty of an offence within s 22(3)` `I contravened section 22` `I had reasonable cause`

-- s 23(1). A corporation may adopt a corporate seal and may change it.
@export May my corporation adopt, and change, a corporate seal (s 23(1))?
GIVEN `the body is a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body a corporation under the Act?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my corporation adopt and change a corporate seal` IF
    `the corporation may adopt, and may change, a corporate seal within s 23(1)` `the body is a corporation`

@export Must my corporation adopt a corporate seal (s 23(1))?
GIVEN `the body is a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body a corporation under the Act?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my corporation adopt a corporate seal` IF
    `the corporation must adopt a corporate seal within s 23(1)` `the body is a corporation`

-- s 23(2). A document executed on behalf of a corporation is not invalid by reason only that a corporate
-- seal is not affixed to it.
@export Is a document I signed for the corporation invalid because no corporate seal is on it (s 23(2))?
GIVEN `I signed on behalf of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the document executed (or, in Quebec, signed) on behalf of the corporation?
      `no corporate seal is on it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is no corporate seal affixed to it?
      `it is invalid on another ground` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document invalid on some other ground?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is a document I signed for the corporation invalid because no corporate seal is on it` IF
    `the document is invalid within s 23(2)` `I signed on behalf of the corporation` `no corporate seal is on it` `it is invalid on another ground`

§§ `Shares, stated capital, series, pre-emptive rights and options (Part V, s 24 to s 29.1)`

-- s 24(1) and (2). Shares of a corporation shall be in registered form and shall be without nominal or par
-- value; a share issued by a body corporate before it was continued under the Act that has a nominal or par
-- value is saved by subsection (2).
@export Is my share in the form the Act requires (s 24(1), (2))?
GIVEN `my share is in registered form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the share in registered form?
      `my share has a nominal or par value` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the share have a nominal or par value?
      `it was issued before my body corporate was continued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the share issued by a body corporate before it was continued under the Act?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my share in the form the Act requires` IF
    `the share is as s 24(1) requires within s 24(1) and s 24(2)` `my share is in registered form` `my share has a nominal or par value` `it was issued before my body corporate was continued`

-- s 24(3). Where a corporation has only one class of shares, the rights of the holders are equal in all
-- respects and include the rights to vote at any meeting of shareholders, to receive any dividend declared,
-- and to receive the remaining property of the corporation on dissolution.
@export As a holder of the only class of shares, do I have this right (s 24(3))?
GIVEN `the corporation has only one class of shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the corporation have only one class of shares?
      `the right` IS A `Right of a holder of shares (s 24(3))` @desc Which right are you asking about?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `As a holder of the only class of shares do I have this right` IS
    `the holders of the only class have the right within s 24(3)` `the corporation has only one class of shares` `the right`

@export Are the rights of the holders of the only class of shares equal in all respects (s 24(3))?
GIVEN `the corporation has only one class of shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the corporation have only one class of shares?
      `the rights are equal in all respects` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the rights of the holders equal in all respects?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are the rights of the holders of the only class of shares equal in all respects` IF
    `the rights of the holders of the only class are as s 24(3) requires` `the corporation has only one class of shares` `the rights are equal in all respects`

-- s 24(4). The articles may provide for more than one class of shares; if they do, the rights, privileges,
-- restrictions and conditions of each class shall be set out in them, and the rights of subsection (3) (to
-- vote, to receive dividends, to receive the remaining property on dissolution) shall be attached to at least
-- one class, though not all to one class.
@export Do my articles meet the requirements for more than one class of shares (s 24(4))?
GIVEN `my articles provide for more than one class` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do your articles provide for more than one class of shares?
      `each class's rights are set out` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the rights, privileges, restrictions and conditions of the shares of each class set out in the articles?
      `a class carries the right to vote` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the right to vote at any meeting of shareholders attached to at least one class?
      `a class carries the right to dividends` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the right to receive any dividend declared attached to at least one class?
      `a class carries the right to the remaining property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the right to receive the remaining property of the corporation on dissolution attached to at least one class?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do my articles meet the requirements for more than one class of shares` IF
    `the articles meet the requirements for classes of shares within s 24(4)` `my articles provide for more than one class` `each class's rights are set out` `a class carries the right to vote` `a class carries the right to dividends` `a class carries the right to the remaining property`

-- s 25(1). Subject to the articles, the by-laws, any unanimous shareholder agreement and section 28, shares
-- may be issued at such times, to such persons and for such consideration as the directors determine.
@export May the directors decide when, to whom and for what consideration shares are issued (s 25(1))?
GIVEN `the articles by-laws or an agreement restrict it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the articles, the by-laws or a unanimous shareholder agreement restrict the directors' determination?
      `shareholders have a pre-emptive right` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 28 restrict the determination because shareholders have a pre-emptive right?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the directors decide when to whom and for what consideration shares are issued` IF
    `the directors may determine the times, persons and consideration of an issue of shares within s 25(1)` `the articles by-laws or an agreement restrict it` `shareholders have a pre-emptive right`

-- s 25(2). Shares issued by a corporation are non-assessable and the holders are not liable to the
-- corporation or to its creditors in respect of them.
@export Am I, as a holder of shares, liable to the corporation or its creditors in respect of them (s 25(2))?
GIVEN `the shares have been issued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the shares been issued by the corporation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I as a holder of shares liable to the corporation or its creditors in respect of them` IS
    `the holder is liable in respect of the share to the corporation or its creditors within s 25(2)` `the shares have been issued`

-- s 25(3). A share shall not be issued until the consideration is fully paid in money or in property or past
-- services that are not less in value than the fair equivalent of the money the corporation would have
-- received had the share been issued for money.
@export May a share be issued for this consideration (s 25(3))?
GIVEN `the consideration` IS A `Kind of consideration for a share (s 25(3))` @desc What is the consideration for the share?
      `it is fully paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the consideration fully paid?
      `its value is at least the fair equivalent of money` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is its value not less than the fair equivalent of the money the corporation would have received had the share been issued for money?
      `the thing is property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the consideration property (leaving aside the exclusion in subsection 25(5) for notes and promises to pay)?
      `it is a note or promise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a promissory note or a promise to pay?
      -- out of range: "arm's length" in the Income Tax Act (outside the Act)
      `it is made by the buyer or a person not at arm's length` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it made by the person to whom the share is issued, or by a person who does not deal at arm's length (within the Income Tax Act) with that person?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May a share be issued for this consideration` IF
    `the share may be issued for the consideration within s 25(3)` `the consideration` `it is fully paid` `its value is at least the fair equivalent of money` (`the thing is property for the purposes of s 25 within s 25(5)` `the thing is property` `it is a note or promise` `it is made by the buyer or a person not at arm's length`)

-- s 25(4). In determining whether property or past services are the fair equivalent of a money consideration,
-- the directors may take into account reasonable charges and expenses of organization and reorganization and
-- payments for property and past services reasonably expected to benefit the corporation.
@export May the directors take this item into account in valuing property or past services (s 25(4))?
GIVEN `the item` IS AN `Item the directors may take into account (s 25(4))` @desc Which item are you asking about?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the directors take this item into account in valuing property or past services` IS
    `the directors may take the item into account in determining the fair equivalent within s 25(4)` `the item`

-- s 25(5). For section 25, property does not include a promissory note, or a promise to pay, made by a person
-- to whom a share is issued, or by a person who does not deal at arm's length with that person.
@export Does this thing count as property when a share is issued for it (s 25(5))?
GIVEN `the thing is property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing property (leaving aside the exclusion in subsection 25(5) for notes and promises to pay)?
      `it is a note or promise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a promissory note or a promise to pay?
      -- out of range: "arm's length" in the Income Tax Act (outside the Act)
      `it is made by the buyer or a person not at arm's length` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it made by the person to whom a share is issued, or by a person who does not deal at arm's length (within the Income Tax Act) with that person?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does this thing count as property when a share is issued for it` IF
    `the thing is property for the purposes of s 25 within s 25(5)` `the thing is property` `it is a note or promise` `it is made by the buyer or a person not at arm's length`

-- s 26(1). A corporation shall maintain a separate stated capital account for each class and series of shares
-- it issues.
@export Does my corporation maintain a separate stated capital account for each class and series (s 26(1))?
GIVEN `we keep a separate account for each class and series` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the corporation maintain a separate stated capital account for each class and series of shares it issues?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my corporation maintain a separate stated capital account for each class and series` IF
    `the corporation has complied with the duty to maintain stated capital accounts within s 26(1)` `we keep a separate account for each class and series`

-- s 26(2), (3) and (4). A corporation shall add to the appropriate stated capital account the full amount of
-- the consideration it receives for shares it issues; but in an exchange of the kinds listed in subsection (3)
-- (non-arm's-length property or shares, arm's-length property with the consent of everyone concerned, or an
-- amalgamation, arrangement or similar transaction) it may add the whole or any part of it; and on the issue
-- of a share it shall not add an amount greater than the consideration it received.
@export May my corporation add this amount to the stated capital account on an issue of shares (s 26(2), (3), (4))?
GIVEN `the consideration we received, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What amount of consideration did the corporation receive for the shares, in dollars?
      `the amount we add, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What amount do you want to add to the stated capital account, in dollars?
      `the exchange` IS AN `Exchange in which shares are issued (s 26(3))` @desc In what kind of exchange are the shares issued?
      `all the people concerned consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the shares are issued in exchange for property of a person dealing at arm's length, do that person, the corporation and all the holders of shares in the class or series so issued consent to the exchange?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my corporation add this amount to the stated capital account on an issue of shares` IF
    `the amount added to the stated capital account is permitted within s 26(2), s 26(3) and s 26(4)` `the consideration we received, in dollars` `the amount we add, in dollars` (`the corporation may add less than the full consideration within s 26(3)` `the exchange` `all the people concerned consent`)

-- s 26(5). Where a corporation proposes to add an amount to a stated capital account that it did not receive as
-- consideration for the issue of shares, and it has outstanding shares of more than one class or series, the
-- addition must be approved by special resolution unless all the issued and outstanding shares are shares of
-- not more than two classes of convertible shares referred to in subsection 39(5).
@export Must my corporation's addition to a stated capital account be approved by special resolution (s 26(5))?
GIVEN `the amount was received as consideration for shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the amount to be added something the corporation received as consideration for the issue of shares?
      `we have outstanding shares of more than one class or series` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the corporation issued outstanding shares of more than one class or series?
      `all the shares are within two convertible classes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are all the issued and outstanding shares shares of not more than two classes of convertible shares referred to in subsection 39(5)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my corporation's addition to a stated capital account be approved by special resolution` IF
    `the addition must be approved by special resolution within s 26(5)` `the amount was received as consideration for shares` `we have outstanding shares of more than one class or series` `all the shares are within two convertible classes`

@export Has my corporation's addition to a stated capital account the approval the Act requires (s 26(5))?
GIVEN `the amount was received as consideration for shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the amount to be added something the corporation received as consideration for the issue of shares?
      `we have outstanding shares of more than one class or series` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the corporation issued outstanding shares of more than one class or series?
      `all the shares are within two convertible classes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are all the issued and outstanding shares shares of not more than two classes of convertible shares referred to in subsection 39(5)?
      `votes for the resolution` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes were cast by shareholders in favour of the resolution?
      `votes against the resolution` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes were cast by shareholders against it?
      `every shareholder signed it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the resolution signed by all the shareholders entitled to vote on it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has my corporation's addition to a stated capital account the approval the Act requires` IF
    `the addition has the approval s 26(5) requires` (`the addition must be approved by special resolution within s 26(5)` `the amount was received as consideration for shares` `we have outstanding shares of more than one class or series` `all the shares are within two convertible classes`) `the tally`
    WHERE
        `the tally` MEANS `Vote tally` WITH
            `votes cast in favour` IS `votes for the resolution`
            `votes cast against` IS `votes against the resolution`
            `signed by all the shareholders entitled to vote on the resolution` IS `every shareholder signed it`

-- s 26(6). When a body corporate is continued under the Act, it may add to a stated capital account any
-- consideration received by it for a share it issued; and a corporation may at any time, subject to
-- subsection (5), add to a stated capital account any amount it credited to a retained earnings or other
-- surplus account.
@export May my corporation add this amount to a stated capital account (s 26(6))?
GIVEN `the amount` IS AN `Amount a corporation proposes to add to a stated capital account (s 26(6))` @desc What is the amount you propose to add?
      `my body corporate was continued under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your body corporate continued under the Act?
      `the addition has the special resolution approval it needs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the addition the approval that subsection 26(5) requires (if it requires any)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my corporation add this amount to a stated capital account` IS
    `the corporation may add the amount to a stated capital account within s 26(6)` `the amount` `my body corporate was continued under the Act` `the addition has the special resolution approval it needs`

-- s 26(7). When a body corporate is continued under the Act, subsection (2) does not apply to consideration it
-- received before it was continued unless the share in respect of which it is received is issued after the
-- continuance.
@export Does the full-amount rule of section 26(2) apply to consideration my continued corporation received earlier (s 26(7))?
GIVEN `my body corporate was continued under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your body corporate continued under the Act?
      `we received the consideration before the continuance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the consideration received before the body corporate was continued?
      `the share was issued after the continuance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the share in respect of which the consideration is received issued after the corporation was continued?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the full-amount rule of section 26(2) apply to consideration my continued corporation received earlier` IF
    `subsection 26(2) applies to the consideration within s 26(7)` `my body corporate was continued under the Act` `we received the consideration before the continuance` `the share was issued after the continuance`

-- s 26(8). When a body corporate is continued under the Act, any amount unpaid on a share issued before the
-- continuance and paid after it shall be added to the stated capital account for that class or series.
@export Must my continued corporation add an amount paid after the continuance to the stated capital account (s 26(8))?
GIVEN `my body corporate was continued under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your body corporate continued under the Act?
      `an amount was unpaid on a share issued before the continuance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was an amount unpaid on a share issued by the body corporate before it was continued?
      `it was paid after the continuance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that amount paid after the body corporate was continued?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my continued corporation add an amount paid after the continuance to the stated capital account` IF
    `the corporation must add the amount to the stated capital account for the class or series within s 26(8)` `my body corporate was continued under the Act` `an amount was unpaid on a share issued before the continuance` `it was paid after the continuance`

-- s 26(9). For the purposes of s 34(2), 38 and 42 and paragraph 185(2)(a), when a body corporate is continued
-- under the Act its stated capital is deemed to include the amount that would have been included in stated
-- capital had it been incorporated under the Act.
@export What is my continued corporation's stated capital for the solvency tests, in dollars (s 26(9))?
GIVEN `my body corporate was continued under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your body corporate continued under the Act?
      `the stated capital in our accounts, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the stated capital shown in the corporation's accounts, in dollars?
      `what it would be had we been incorporated under the Act, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What amount would have been included in stated capital had the body corporate been incorporated under the Act, in dollars?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my continued corporation's stated capital for the solvency tests` IS
    `the stated capital of the body corporate for the purposes of s 34(2), s 38, s 42 and paragraph 185(2)(a) within s 26(9)` `my body corporate was continued under the Act` `the stated capital in our accounts, in dollars` `what it would be had we been incorporated under the Act, in dollars`

-- s 26(10). A corporation shall not reduce its stated capital or any stated capital account except in the
-- manner provided in the Act.
@export May my corporation reduce its stated capital or a stated capital account in this way (s 26(10))?
GIVEN `the reduction is in a manner the Act provides` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the reduction made in a manner provided in the Act (for example by special resolution under section 38, or on a purchase or redemption of shares under sections 34 to 36)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my corporation reduce its stated capital or a stated capital account in this way` IF
    `the corporation may reduce its stated capital or a stated capital account within s 26(10)` `the reduction is in a manner the Act provides`

-- s 26(11) and (12). The stated capital provisions do not apply to an open-end mutual fund: a distributing
-- corporation that carries on only the business of investing the consideration it receives for the shares it
-- issues, all or substantially all of which are redeemable on the demand of a shareholder.
@export Is my corporation an open-end mutual fund (s 26(12))?
GIVEN
      -- out of range: section 2(1) (keel)
      `it is a distributing corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation a distributing corporation?
      `it only invests what it receives for its shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it carry on only the business of investing the consideration it receives for the shares it issues?
      `its shares are redeemable on demand` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are all or substantially all of its shares redeemable on the demand of a shareholder?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my corporation an open-end mutual fund` IF
    `the corporation is an open-end mutual fund within s 26(12)` `it is a distributing corporation` `it only invests what it receives for its shares` `its shares are redeemable on demand`

@export Do the stated capital provisions of the Act apply to my corporation (s 26(11))?
GIVEN
      -- out of range: section 2(1) (keel)
      `it is a distributing corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation a distributing corporation?
      `it only invests what it receives for its shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it carry on only the business of investing the consideration it receives for the shares it issues?
      `its shares are redeemable on demand` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are all or substantially all of its shares redeemable on the demand of a shareholder?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do the stated capital provisions of the Act apply to my corporation` IF
    `the stated capital provisions of this Act apply to the corporation within s 26(11)` (`the corporation is an open-end mutual fund within s 26(12)` `it is a distributing corporation` `it only invests what it receives for its shares` `its shares are redeemable on demand`)

-- s 27(1). The articles may authorize the issue of a class of shares in series, and may fix the number,
-- designation and rights of each series themselves, or authorize the directors to do so.
@export May my articles authorize a class of shares in series in this way (s 27(1))?
GIVEN `the way` IS A `Way of fixing the terms of a series (s 27(1))` @desc How do the articles fix the terms of the series?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my articles authorize a class of shares in series in this way` IF
    `the articles may authorize the issue of a class of shares in series in that way within s 27(1)` `the way`

-- s 27(2). If cumulative dividends or amounts payable on return of capital on a series are not paid in full,
-- the shares of all series of the same class participate rateably in respect of the accumulated dividends and
-- the return of capital.
@export How much does my series of shares receive when what is owing is not paid in full, in dollars (s 27(2))?
GIVEN `the sum available, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What sum is available for the accumulated dividends or the return of capital, in dollars?
      `the amount owing to my series, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What amount is owing to your series, in dollars?
      `the amount owing to all series of the class, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What amount is owing to all series of the same class, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much does my series of shares receive when what is owing is not paid in full` IS
    `the amount this series receives within s 27(2)` `the sum available, in dollars` `the amount owing to my series, in dollars` `the amount owing to all series of the class, in dollars`

-- s 27(3). No rights, privileges, restrictions or conditions attached to a series shall confer a priority in
-- respect of dividends or return of capital over any other series of the same class that are then outstanding.
@export May the rights attached to my series give it priority over another series of the same class (s 27(3))?
GIVEN `the rights give my series a priority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the rights, privileges, restrictions or conditions attached to the series confer on it a priority in respect of dividends or return of capital over another series of the same class that is then outstanding?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the rights attached to my series give it priority over another series of the same class` IF
    `the rights attached to the series are permitted within s 27(3)` `the rights give my series a priority`

-- s 27(4). If the directors exercise their authority under paragraph 27(1)(b), they shall, before the issue
-- of shares of the series, send articles of amendment designating the series to the Director in the Director's
-- form.
@export Have the directors sent the articles of amendment designating the series before issuing the shares (s 27(4))?
GIVEN `the directors fix the series under their authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the directors exercising their authority under paragraph 27(1)(b) to fix the terms of a series?
      `the day the articles of amendment were sent` IS A DATE @desc On what day were the articles of amendment designating the series sent to the Director?
      `the day the shares were issued` IS A DATE @desc On what day were shares of the series issued?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have the directors sent the articles of amendment designating the series before issuing the shares` IF
    `the directors have complied with the duty to send articles of amendment before the issue within s 27(4)` `the directors fix the series under their authority` `the day the articles of amendment were sent` `the day the shares were issued`

-- s 27(5). On receipt of articles of amendment designating a series, the Director shall issue a certificate of
-- amendment in accordance with section 262.
@export Must the Director issue a certificate of amendment for my series of shares (s 27(5))?
GIVEN `the Director has received the articles of amendment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Director received articles of amendment designating a series of shares?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the Director issue a certificate of amendment for my series of shares` IF
    `the Director must issue a certificate of amendment within s 27(5)` `the Director has received the articles of amendment`

-- s 27(6). The articles are amended on the date shown in the certificate of amendment.
@export Have my articles been amended to designate the series on this day (s 27(6))?
GIVEN `the date shown in the certificate of amendment` IS A DATE @desc What date is shown in the certificate of amendment?
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you want to know whether the articles are amended?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have my articles been amended to designate the series on this day` IF
    `the articles are amended by the certificate of amendment by the day within s 27(6)` `the date shown in the certificate of amendment` `the day I am asking about`

-- s 28(1) and (2). If the articles so provide, no shares of a class shall be issued unless first offered to the
-- shareholders holding shares of that class, who have a pre-emptive right to acquire them in proportion to
-- their holdings, at the price and on the terms on which they are to be offered to others; but there is no
-- pre-emptive right in respect of shares issued for a consideration other than money, as a share dividend, or
-- on the exercise of conversion privileges, options or rights previously granted by the corporation.
@export Do I, as a shareholder, have a pre-emptive right in respect of this issue of shares (s 28(1), (2))?
GIVEN `my articles provide a pre-emptive right` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the articles provide for the pre-emptive right?
      `the issue` IS AN `Issue of shares (s 28(2))` @desc What kind of issue of shares is it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I as a shareholder have a pre-emptive right in respect of this issue of shares` IF
    `shareholders of the class have a pre-emptive right in respect of the shares within s 28(1) and s 28(2)` `my articles provide a pre-emptive right` `the issue`

@export How many of the offered shares do I have a pre-emptive right to acquire (s 28(1))?
GIVEN `the number of shares offered` IS A NUMBER @desc How many shares of the class are offered?
      `the number of shares of the class I hold` IS A NUMBER @desc How many shares of the class do you hold?
      `the number of shares of the class all shareholders hold` IS A NUMBER @desc How many shares of the class do all shareholders hold?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How many of the offered shares do I have a pre-emptive right to acquire` IS
    `the number of the offered shares the shareholder has a pre-emptive right to acquire within s 28(1)` `the number of shares offered` `the number of shares of the class I hold` `the number of shares of the class all shareholders hold`

@export May the corporation issue these shares of the class without first offering them to the shareholders (s 28(1), (2))?
GIVEN `my articles provide a pre-emptive right` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the articles provide for the pre-emptive right?
      `the issue` IS AN `Issue of shares (s 28(2))` @desc What kind of issue of shares is it?
      `the shares were first offered to the holders of the class` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the shares first been offered to the shareholders holding shares of that class, at the price and on the terms on which they are to be offered to others?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the corporation issue these shares of the class without first offering them to the shareholders` IF
    `the shares of the class may be issued within s 28(1)` `my articles provide a pre-emptive right` `the shares were first offered to the holders of the class` `the issue is within the exceptions`
    WHERE
        `the issue is within the exceptions` MEANS NOT (`shareholders of the class have a pre-emptive right in respect of the shares within s 28(1) and s 28(2)` TRUE `the issue`)

-- s 29(1). A corporation may issue certificates, warrants or other evidences of conversion privileges,
-- options or rights to acquire its securities, and shall set out the conditions in them or in the certificates
-- of the securities to which they are attached.
@export Has my corporation set out the conditions of its options and conversion rights where the Act requires (s 29(1))?
GIVEN `the conditions are in the warrants or other evidences` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the conditions set out in the certificates, warrants or other evidences of the conversion privileges, options or rights?
      `the conditions are in the securities' certificates` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the conditions set out in the certificates evidencing the securities to which the privileges, options or rights are attached?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has my corporation set out the conditions of its options and conversion rights where the Act requires` IF
    `the corporation has set out the conditions as s 29(1) requires` `the conditions are in the warrants or other evidences` `the conditions are in the securities' certificates`

-- s 29(2). Conversion privileges, options and rights to acquire securities may be made transferable or
-- non-transferable, and options and rights to acquire may be made separable or inseparable from the securities
-- to which they are attached.
@export May my corporation make this conversion privilege, option or right transferable or non-transferable (s 29(2))?
GIVEN `the instrument` IS AN `Instrument under s 29(2)` @desc What kind of instrument is it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my corporation make this conversion privilege option or right transferable or non-transferable` IF
    `the instrument may be made transferable or non-transferable within s 29(2)` `the instrument`

@export May my corporation make this option or right separable or inseparable from the securities it is attached to (s 29(2))?
GIVEN `the instrument` IS AN `Instrument under s 29(2)` @desc What kind of instrument is it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my corporation make this option or right separable or inseparable from the securities it is attached to` IS
    `the instrument may be made separable or inseparable from the securities to which it is attached within s 29(2)` `the instrument`

-- s 29(3). Where the corporation has granted conversion privileges or issued options or rights to acquire
-- shares and the articles limit the number of authorized shares, it shall reserve, and continue to reserve,
-- sufficient authorized shares to meet their exercise.
@export Has my corporation reserved enough authorized shares to meet the exercise of its conversion privileges, options and rights (s 29(3))?
GIVEN `my articles limit the authorized shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the articles limit the number of authorized shares?
      `the number of authorized shares` IS A NUMBER @desc How many shares are authorized?
      `the number of shares issued` IS A NUMBER @desc How many shares have been issued?
      `the number needed for the conversion privileges, options and rights` IS A NUMBER @desc How many shares are needed to meet the exercise of the conversion privileges, options and rights?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has my corporation reserved enough authorized shares to meet the exercise of its conversion privileges options and rights` IF
    `the corporation has reserved sufficient authorized shares within s 29(3)` `my articles limit the authorized shares` `the number of authorized shares` `the number of shares issued` `the number needed for the conversion privileges, options and rights`

-- s 29.1(1). Despite section 29, a corporation shall not issue, in bearer form, a certificate, warrant or other
-- evidence of a conversion privilege, option or right to acquire a share.
@export Is my corporation forbidden to issue this document in bearer form (s 29.1(1))?
GIVEN `it is a certificate warrant or other evidence of a right to acquire a share` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document a certificate, warrant or other evidence of a conversion privilege, option or right to acquire a share of the corporation?
      `it is in bearer form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it in bearer form?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my corporation forbidden to issue this document in bearer form` IF
    `the corporation is forbidden to issue the document within s 29.1(1)` `it is a certificate warrant or other evidence of a right to acquire a share` `it is in bearer form`

-- s 29.1(2). On the request of a holder of such a document in bearer form issued before section 29.1 came
-- into force, the corporation shall issue in exchange a certificate, warrant or other evidence in registered
-- form.
@export Must the corporation exchange my bearer-form certificate for a registered one when I ask (s 29.1(2))?
GIVEN `I asked for an exchange` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you asked the corporation to exchange the document?
      `it is a bearer form certificate warrant or other evidence of a right to acquire a share` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document a certificate, warrant or other evidence of a conversion privilege, option or right to acquire a share of the corporation, in bearer form?
      -- out of range: the day section 29.1 came into force (not in the text)
      `it was issued before section 29.1 came into force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it issued before the coming into force of section 29.1?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the corporation exchange my bearer-form certificate for a registered one when I ask` IF
    `the corporation must issue a registered document in exchange within s 29.1(2)` `I asked for an exchange` `it is a bearer form certificate warrant or other evidence of a right to acquire a share` `it was issued before section 29.1 came into force`

§§ `The corporation holding or buying its own shares (Part V, s 30 to s 37)`

-- This group arises only when the corporation, or one of its subsidiaries, holds or acquires shares of the
-- corporation, or when the corporation buys or redeems its own shares: the form may ask "Is your corporation
-- holding, buying or redeeming its own shares?" before showing it.

-- s 31(1). A corporation may, in the capacity of a personal representative, hold shares in itself or in its
-- holding body corporate unless it, the holding body corporate or a subsidiary of either has a beneficial
-- interest in the shares.
@export May my corporation hold shares in itself as a personal representative (s 31(1))?
GIVEN `we hold the shares as a personal representative` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the corporation hold the shares in the capacity of a personal representative?
      -- out of range: section 2(4) (keel)
      `we or a related body has a beneficial interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the corporation, the holding body corporate or a subsidiary of either have a beneficial interest in the shares?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my corporation hold shares in itself as a personal representative` IF
    `section 31(1) permits the corporation to hold the shares` `we hold the shares as a personal representative` `we or a related body has a beneficial interest`

-- s 31(2). A corporation may hold shares in itself or in its holding body corporate by way of security for the
-- purposes of a transaction entered into by it in the ordinary course of a business that includes the lending
-- of money.
@export May my corporation hold shares in itself by way of security (s 31(2))?
GIVEN `we hold the shares by way of security` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the corporation hold the shares by way of security?
      `it is for a transaction in our ordinary lending business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the security for the purposes of a transaction entered into by the corporation in the ordinary course of a business that includes the lending of money?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my corporation hold shares in itself by way of security` IF
    `section 31(2) permits the corporation to hold the shares` `we hold the shares by way of security` `it is for a transaction in our ordinary lending business`

-- s 32(1). Subject to s 39(8), a corporation may, to assist itself or its affiliates or associates to qualify
-- under a prescribed law of Canada or a province for licences, permits, grants, payments or other benefits by
-- reason of a specified level of Canadian ownership or control, hold shares in itself that (a) are not
-- constrained for that purpose, or (b) are shares into which such shares were converted by it, are constrained
-- for that purpose and were not previously held by it.
@export May my corporation hold shares in itself to meet a Canadian ownership requirement (s 32(1))?
GIVEN
      -- out of range: the regulations (not among the sources)
      `the purpose is a Canadian ownership qualification` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the purpose to assist the corporation or any of its affiliates or associates to qualify under a prescribed law of Canada or a province to receive licences, permits, grants, payments or other benefits by reason of attaining or maintaining a specified level of Canadian ownership or control?
      `the shares are not constrained for that purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the shares not constrained for that purpose?
      `the shares are converted constrained shares not previously held` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they shares into which shares held under paragraph 32(1)(a) were converted by the corporation, that are constrained for that purpose and were not previously held by the corporation?
      `the two years of subsection 39(8) have run` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have two years run (subsection 39(8)) with the corporation still holding the shares, so that subsection 39(8) forbids it to hold them?
