    `section 32(1) permits the corporation to hold the shares` `the purpose is a Canadian ownership qualification` `the shares are not constrained for that purpose` `the shares are converted constrained shares not previously held` `the two years of subsection 39(8) have run`

-- s 30(1)(a). Subject to s 30(2) and sections 31 to 36, a corporation shall not hold shares in itself or in its
-- holding body corporate. The exceptions are those of s 31(1), s 31(2) and s 32(1).
@export May my corporation hold shares in itself or in its holding body corporate (s 30(1)(a))?
GIVEN `we hold the shares as a personal representative` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the corporation hold the shares in the capacity of a personal representative?
      -- out of range: section 2(4) (keel)
      `we or a related body has a beneficial interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the corporation, the holding body corporate or a subsidiary of either have a beneficial interest in the shares?
      `we hold the shares by way of security` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the corporation hold the shares by way of security?
      `it is for a transaction in our ordinary lending business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the security for the purposes of a transaction entered into by the corporation in the ordinary course of a business that includes the lending of money?
      -- out of range: the regulations (not among the sources)
      `the purpose is a Canadian ownership qualification` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the purpose to assist the corporation or any of its affiliates or associates to qualify under a prescribed law of Canada or a province for benefits by reason of a specified level of Canadian ownership or control?
      `the shares are not constrained for that purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the shares not constrained for that purpose?
      `the shares are converted constrained shares not previously held` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they shares into which shares held under paragraph 32(1)(a) were converted by the corporation, that are constrained for that purpose and were not previously held by the corporation?
      `the two years of subsection 39(8) have run` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have two years run (subsection 39(8)) with the corporation still holding the shares?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my corporation hold shares in itself or in its holding body corporate` IF
    `the corporation may hold shares in itself or in its holding body corporate within s 30(1)(a)` (`section 31(1) permits the corporation to hold the shares` `we hold the shares as a personal representative` `we or a related body has a beneficial interest`) (`section 31(2) permits the corporation to hold the shares` `we hold the shares by way of security` `it is for a transaction in our ordinary lending business`) (`section 32(1) permits the corporation to hold the shares` `the purpose is a Canadian ownership qualification` `the shares are not constrained for that purpose` `the shares are converted constrained shares not previously held` `the two years of subsection 39(8) have run`)

-- s 31(3). A corporation may permit a subsidiary to acquire shares of the corporation (a) in the subsidiary's
-- capacity as a personal representative, unless the subsidiary would have a beneficial interest, or (b) by way
-- of security for a transaction in the subsidiary's ordinary lending business.
@export May my corporation permit its subsidiary to acquire shares of the corporation as a personal representative or by way of security (s 31(3))?
