      -- out of range: section 2(4) (keel)
      `the subsidiary would have a beneficial interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the subsidiary have a beneficial interest in the shares?
      `the subsidiary acquires by way of security` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the subsidiary acquire the shares by way of security?
      `it is for the subsidiary's ordinary lending business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the security for the purposes of a transaction entered into by the subsidiary in the ordinary course of a business that includes the lending of money?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my corporation permit its subsidiary to acquire shares of the corporation as a personal representative or by way of security` IF
    `section 31(3) permits the corporation to permit the subsidiary to acquire the shares` `the subsidiary acquires as a personal representative` `the subsidiary would have a beneficial interest` `the subsidiary acquires by way of security` `it is for the subsidiary's ordinary lending business`

-- s 31(4). A corporation may permit a subsidiary to acquire shares of the corporation through their issuance by
-- the corporation to it if, before the acquisition, the conditions prescribed for subsection (4) are met.
@export May my corporation permit its subsidiary to acquire shares of the corporation through their issuance to it (s 31(4))?
