      -- out of range: the regulations (not among the sources)
      `the prescribed conditions were met beforehand` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the conditions prescribed for subsection 31(4) met before the acquisition took place?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my corporation permit its subsidiary to acquire shares of the corporation through their issuance to it` IF
    `section 31(4) permits the corporation to permit the subsidiary to acquire the shares` `the subsidiary acquires by issuance from us` `the prescribed conditions were met beforehand`

-- s 31(5). After an acquisition has taken place under the purported authority of subsection (4), the
-- conditions prescribed for subsection (5) must be met.
@export Are the conditions that must be met after a subsidiary's acquisition by issuance satisfied (s 31(5))?
