      -- out of range: the regulations (not among the sources)
      `an after-condition is not met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are one or more of the conditions prescribed for subsection 31(5) not met, or did they cease to be met?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do the prescribed consequences apply to my subsidiary's acquisition of shares of the corporation` IF
    `the prescribed consequences apply to the acquisition and issuance within s 31(6)` `we permitted the acquisition under subsection 31(4)` `a before-condition was not met` `an after-condition is not met`

-- s 30(1)(b). Subject to s 30(2) and sections 31 to 36, a corporation shall not permit a subsidiary to acquire
-- shares of the corporation. The exceptions are those of s 31(3) and s 31(4).
