-- s 30(2). Subject to section 31, a corporation shall cause a subsidiary that holds shares of the corporation to
-- sell or otherwise dispose of them within five years from the date (a) the body corporate became a subsidiary of
-- the corporation or (b) the corporation was continued under the Act.
@export By what day must my corporation's subsidiary dispose of the shares it holds in the corporation (s 30(2))?
GIVEN `section 31 lets the subsidiary keep the shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 31 permit the subsidiary to hold the shares?
      `the day it became our subsidiary` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the body corporate become a subsidiary of the corporation?
      `we were continued under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the corporation continued under the Act?
      `the day we were continued` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the corporation continued? (any date if it was not)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `By what day must my corporation's subsidiary dispose of the shares it holds in the corporation` IS
    `the last day for the subsidiary to dispose of the shares within s 30(2)` `section 31 lets the subsidiary keep the shares` `the day it became our subsidiary` `the day we were continued if we were`
    WHERE
        `the day we were continued if we were` MEANS IF `we were continued under the Act` THEN JUST `the day we were continued` ELSE NOTHING

-- s 32(2). A corporation shall not transfer shares held under subsection 32(1) to any person unless it is
-- satisfied, on reasonable grounds, that the ownership of the shares as a result of the transfer would assist
-- it or its affiliates or associates to achieve the purpose set out in subsection 32(1).
@export May my corporation transfer shares it holds under the Canadian ownership exception (s 32(2))?
GIVEN `we are satisfied on reasonable grounds the transfer would assist` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation satisfied, on reasonable grounds, that the ownership of the shares as a result of the transfer would assist it or any of its affiliates or associates to achieve the purpose set out in subsection 32(1)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my corporation transfer shares it holds under the Canadian ownership exception` IF
    `the corporation may transfer the shares held under subsection 32(1) within s 32(2)` `we are satisfied on reasonable grounds the transfer would assist`

-- s 32(3). A corporation that, without reasonable cause, fails to comply with subsection (2) is guilty of an
-- offence and liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding five thousand dollars.
@export Is my corporation guilty of an offence for transferring such shares without being satisfied (s 32(3))?
GIVEN `we failed to comply with subsection 32(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the corporation failed to comply with subsection 32(2)?
      `we had reasonable cause` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the corporation have reasonable cause?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my corporation guilty of an offence for transferring such shares without being satisfied` IF
    `the corporation is guilty of an offence within s 32(3)` `we failed to comply with subsection 32(2)` `we had reasonable cause`

-- s 32(4). Where a corporation commits an offence under subsection (3), any director who knowingly
-- authorized, permitted or acquiesced in it is a party to and guilty of the offence, liable on summary
-- conviction to a fine not exceeding five thousand dollars or imprisonment not exceeding six months or both,
-- whether or not the corporation has been prosecuted or convicted.
@export Am I, as a director, guilty of the offence my corporation committed under subsection 32(3) (s 32(4))?
GIVEN `the corporation committed an offence under subsection 32(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the corporation commit an offence under subsection 32(3)?
      `I am a director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director of the corporation?
      `I knowingly authorized, permitted or acquiesced` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you knowingly authorize, permit or acquiesce in the commission of the offence?
      `the corporation has been prosecuted or convicted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the corporation been prosecuted or convicted?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I as a director guilty of the offence my corporation committed under subsection 32(3)` IF
    `the director is a party to and guilty of the offence within s 32(4)` `the corporation committed an offence under subsection 32(3)` `I am a director` `I knowingly authorized, permitted or acquiesced` `the corporation has been prosecuted or convicted`

-- s 32(5). Where shares held under subsection (1) are transferred by the corporation, subsections 25(1), (3),
-- (4) and (5), paragraph 115(3)(c) and subsection 118(1) apply, with such modifications as the circumstances
-- require, as if the transfer were an issue.
