      `there are grounds to believe we cannot pay our debts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are there reasonable grounds for believing that the corporation is, or would after the payment be, unable to pay its liabilities as they become due?
      `the realizable value of our assets after the payment, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What would the realizable value of the corporation's assets be after the payment, in dollars?
      `our liabilities, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What are the corporation's liabilities, in dollars?
      `the amount payable rateably or first on redemption or liquidation, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What amount would be required, on a redemption or in a liquidation, to pay the holders of shares that have a right to be paid rateably with or before the holders of the shares to be purchased or redeemed, to the extent not already included in the liabilities, in dollars?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my corporation purchase or redeem redeemable shares at this price` IF
    `the corporation may purchase or redeem the shares at the price within s 36(1)` `the shares are redeemable` `the price per share, in dollars` `the redemption price per share, in dollars` `my articles forbid it` (`the corporation is forbidden to make the payment to purchase or redeem redeemable shares within s 36(2)` `the solvency facts`)
    WHERE
        `the solvency facts` MEANS `Facts for a solvency test in Part V` WITH
            -- Placeholders: the s 36(2) rule does not read the stated capital, the amount owed first, or the fund flag.
            `reasonable grounds exist for believing that the corporation is, or would after the step be, unable to pay its liabilities as they become due` IS `there are grounds to believe we cannot pay our debts`
            `realizable value of the corporation's assets after the step, in dollars` IS `the realizable value of our assets after the payment, in dollars`
            `liabilities of the corporation, in dollars` IS `our liabilities, in dollars`
            `stated capital of all classes, in dollars` IS 0
            `amount required, on a redemption or in a liquidation, to pay the holders of shares that must be paid before the shares to be acquired and not included in the liabilities, in dollars` IS 0
            `amount required, on a redemption or in a liquidation, to pay the holders of shares that must be paid rateably with or before the shares to be acquired and not included in the liabilities, in dollars` IS `the amount payable rateably or first on redemption or liquidation, in dollars`
            `the corporation is an open-end mutual fund` IS FALSE

-- s 36(2). A corporation shall not make any payment to purchase or redeem any redeemable shares issued by it if
-- there are reasonable grounds for believing that (a) it is, or would after the payment be, unable to pay its
-- liabilities as they become due, or (b) the realizable value of its assets would after the payment be less
-- than the aggregate of (i) its liabilities and (ii) the amount that would be required to pay the holders of
-- shares that have a right to be paid, on a redemption or in a liquidation, rateably with or before the holders
-- of the shares to be purchased or redeemed, to the extent not included in its liabilities.
@export Is my corporation forbidden to pay to purchase or redeem redeemable shares (s 36(2))?
GIVEN `there are grounds to believe we cannot pay our debts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are there reasonable grounds for believing that the corporation is, or would after the payment be, unable to pay its liabilities as they become due?
      `the realizable value of our assets after the payment, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What would the realizable value of the corporation's assets be after the payment, in dollars?
      `our liabilities, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What are the corporation's liabilities, in dollars?
      `the amount payable rateably or first on redemption or liquidation, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What amount would be required, on a redemption or in a liquidation, to pay the holders of shares that have a right to be paid rateably with or before the holders of the shares to be purchased or redeemed, to the extent not already included in the liabilities, in dollars?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my corporation forbidden to pay to purchase or redeem redeemable shares` IF
    `the corporation is forbidden to make the payment to purchase or redeem redeemable shares within s 36(2)` `the solvency facts`
    WHERE
        `the solvency facts` MEANS `Facts for a solvency test in Part V` WITH
            -- Placeholders: the s 36(2) rule does not read the stated capital, the amount owed first, or the fund flag.
            `reasonable grounds exist for believing that the corporation is, or would after the step be, unable to pay its liabilities as they become due` IS `there are grounds to believe we cannot pay our debts`
            `realizable value of the corporation's assets after the step, in dollars` IS `the realizable value of our assets after the payment, in dollars`
            `liabilities of the corporation, in dollars` IS `our liabilities, in dollars`
            `stated capital of all classes, in dollars` IS 0
            `amount required, on a redemption or in a liquidation, to pay the holders of shares that must be paid before the shares to be acquired and not included in the liabilities, in dollars` IS 0
            `amount required, on a redemption or in a liquidation, to pay the holders of shares that must be paid rateably with or before the shares to be acquired and not included in the liabilities, in dollars` IS `the amount payable rateably or first on redemption or liquidation, in dollars`
            `the corporation is an open-end mutual fund` IS FALSE

-- s 37. A corporation may accept from any shareholder a share of the corporation surrendered to it as a gift
-- (in Quebec, including a legacy), but may not extinguish or reduce a liability in respect of an amount unpaid
-- on any such share except in accordance with section 38.
@export May my corporation accept a share surrendered to it as a gift (s 37)?
GIVEN `a shareholder surrendered the share as a gift` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the share surrendered to the corporation by a shareholder as a gift (or, in Quebec, a legacy)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my corporation accept a share surrendered to it as a gift` IF
    `the corporation may accept the share within s 37` `a shareholder surrendered the share as a gift`

@export May my corporation extinguish or reduce a liability for an amount unpaid on a share surrendered to it (s 37)?
GIVEN `we extinguish or reduce a liability for an unpaid amount` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the corporation extinguish or reduce a liability in respect of an amount unpaid on the share?
      `we do so in accordance with section 38` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it do so in accordance with section 38?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my corporation extinguish or reduce a liability for an amount unpaid on a share surrendered to it` IF
    `the corporation may extinguish or reduce the liability within s 37` `we extinguish or reduce a liability for an unpaid amount` `we do so in accordance with section 38`

§§ `Reducing stated capital, adjusting it, dividends and shareholder liability (Part V, s 38 to s 45)`

-- s 38(1). Subject to subsection (3), a corporation may by special resolution reduce its stated capital for any
-- purpose, including (a) extinguishing or reducing a liability in respect of an amount unpaid on any share, (b)
-- distributing to the holder of an issued share an amount not exceeding the stated capital of the class or
-- series, and (c) declaring its stated capital to be reduced by an amount that is not represented by realizable
-- assets. A special resolution is passed by at least two thirds of the votes cast, or signed by all the
-- shareholders entitled to vote.
@export May my corporation reduce its stated capital by special resolution for this purpose (s 38(1))?
GIVEN `the purpose` IS A `Purpose of a reduction of stated capital (s 38(1))` @desc For what purpose does the corporation want to reduce its stated capital?
      `votes for the resolution` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes were cast by shareholders in favour of the resolution?
      `votes against the resolution` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes were cast by shareholders against it?
      `every shareholder signed it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the resolution signed by all the shareholders entitled to vote on it?
      `there are grounds to believe we cannot pay our debts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are there reasonable grounds for believing that the corporation is, or would after the reduction be, unable to pay its liabilities as they become due?
      `the realizable value of our assets after the reduction, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What would the realizable value of the corporation's assets be after the reduction, in dollars?
      `our liabilities, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What are the corporation's liabilities, in dollars?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my corporation reduce its stated capital by special resolution for this purpose` IF
    `the corporation may reduce its stated capital within s 38(1)` `the tally` (`the corporation is forbidden to reduce its stated capital within s 38(3)` `the purpose` `the solvency facts`)
    WHERE
        `the tally` MEANS `Vote tally` WITH
            `votes cast in favour` IS `votes for the resolution`
            `votes cast against` IS `votes against the resolution`
            `signed by all the shareholders entitled to vote on the resolution` IS `every shareholder signed it`
        `the solvency facts` MEANS `Facts for a solvency test in Part V` WITH
            -- Placeholders: the s 38(3) rule reads only the grounds, the assets and the liabilities.
            `reasonable grounds exist for believing that the corporation is, or would after the step be, unable to pay its liabilities as they become due` IS `there are grounds to believe we cannot pay our debts`
            `realizable value of the corporation's assets after the step, in dollars` IS `the realizable value of our assets after the reduction, in dollars`
            `liabilities of the corporation, in dollars` IS `our liabilities, in dollars`
            `stated capital of all classes, in dollars` IS 0
            `amount required, on a redemption or in a liquidation, to pay the holders of shares that must be paid before the shares to be acquired and not included in the liabilities, in dollars` IS 0
            `amount required, on a redemption or in a liquidation, to pay the holders of shares that must be paid rateably with or before the shares to be acquired and not included in the liabilities, in dollars` IS 0
            `the corporation is an open-end mutual fund` IS FALSE

-- s 38(1)(b). A distribution to the holder of an issued share may not exceed the stated capital of the class
-- or series.
@export Is the amount my corporation distributes to a shareholder within the stated capital of the class or series (s 38(1)(b))?
GIVEN `the amount distributed to the holder, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What amount is distributed to the holder of an issued share, in dollars?
      `the stated capital of the class or series, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the stated capital of the class or series, in dollars?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the amount my corporation distributes to a shareholder within the stated capital of the class or series` IF
    `the distribution is within the limit of s 38(1)(b)` `the amount distributed to the holder, in dollars` `the stated capital of the class or series, in dollars`

-- s 38(2). A special resolution under section 38 shall specify the stated capital account or accounts from which
-- the reduction will be deducted.
@export Does our special resolution to reduce stated capital say what the Act requires (s 38(2))?
GIVEN `it names the stated capital accounts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the special resolution specify the stated capital account or accounts from which the reduction will be deducted?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does our special resolution to reduce stated capital say what the Act requires` IF
    `the special resolution has the contents s 38(2) requires` `it names the stated capital accounts`

-- s 38(3). A corporation shall not reduce its stated capital for any purpose other than the purpose in
-- paragraph (1)(c) if there are reasonable grounds for believing that (a) it is, or would after the reduction be,
-- unable to pay its liabilities as they become due, or (b) the realizable value of its assets would thereby be
-- less than its liabilities.
@export Is my corporation forbidden to reduce its stated capital for this purpose (s 38(3))?
GIVEN `the purpose` IS A `Purpose of a reduction of stated capital (s 38(1))` @desc For what purpose does the corporation want to reduce its stated capital?
      `there are grounds to believe we cannot pay our debts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are there reasonable grounds for believing that the corporation is, or would after the reduction be, unable to pay its liabilities as they become due?
      `the realizable value of our assets after the reduction, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What would the realizable value of the corporation's assets be after the reduction, in dollars?
      `our liabilities, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What are the corporation's liabilities, in dollars?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my corporation forbidden to reduce its stated capital for this purpose` IF
    `the corporation is forbidden to reduce its stated capital within s 38(3)` `the purpose` `the solvency facts`
    WHERE
        `the solvency facts` MEANS `Facts for a solvency test in Part V` WITH
            -- Placeholders: the s 38(3) rule reads only the grounds, the assets and the liabilities.
            `reasonable grounds exist for believing that the corporation is, or would after the step be, unable to pay its liabilities as they become due` IS `there are grounds to believe we cannot pay our debts`
            `realizable value of the corporation's assets after the step, in dollars` IS `the realizable value of our assets after the reduction, in dollars`
            `liabilities of the corporation, in dollars` IS `our liabilities, in dollars`
            `stated capital of all classes, in dollars` IS 0
            `amount required, on a redemption or in a liquidation, to pay the holders of shares that must be paid before the shares to be acquired and not included in the liabilities, in dollars` IS 0
            `amount required, on a redemption or in a liquidation, to pay the holders of shares that must be paid rateably with or before the shares to be acquired and not included in the liabilities, in dollars` IS 0
            `the corporation is an open-end mutual fund` IS FALSE

-- s 38(4). A creditor of a corporation is entitled to apply to a court for an order compelling a shareholder or
-- other recipient (a) to pay the corporation an amount equal to any liability of the shareholder that was
-- extinguished or reduced contrary to section 38, or (b) to pay or deliver to the corporation any money or
-- property paid or distributed as a consequence of a reduction of capital made contrary to section 38.
@export Can a creditor apply to a court for an order against me as a shareholder who received something under a reduction of capital (s 38(4))?
GIVEN `the order` IS AN `Order a creditor may seek under s 38(4)` @desc Which order does the creditor seek?
      `the applicant is a creditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the applicant a creditor of the corporation?
      `the act contrary to section 38 was done` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the act that the order is about (a liability extinguished or reduced, or a payment or distribution made as a consequence of a reduction of capital) done contrary to section 38?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can a creditor apply to a court for an order against me as a shareholder who received something under a reduction of capital` IF
    `the creditor is entitled to apply to a court for the order within s 38(4)` `the order` `the applicant is a creditor` `the act contrary to section 38 was done`

-- s 38(5). An action to enforce a liability imposed by section 38 may not be commenced after two years from the
-- date of the act complained of.
@export By what day must an action to enforce a liability under section 38 be commenced (s 38(5))?
GIVEN `the date of the act complained of` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the act complained of done?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what day must an action to enforce a liability under section 38 be commenced` IS
    `the last day to commence an action to enforce a liability imposed by section 38 within s 38(5)` `the date of the act complained of`

@export Is an action to enforce a liability under section 38 in time (s 38(5))?
GIVEN `the date of the act complained of` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the act complained of done?
      `the day the action was commenced` IS A DATE @desc On what day was (or will) the action be commenced?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is an action to enforce a liability under section 38 in time` IF
    `the action to enforce a liability imposed by section 38 is in time within s 38(5)` `the date of the act complained of` `the day the action was commenced`

-- s 39(1). On a purchase, redemption or other acquisition by a corporation of its shares (under s 34, 35, 36,
-- 45 or 190 or paragraph 241(3)(f)), it shall deduct from the stated capital account for the class or series the
-- stated capital of the shares of that class or series multiplied by the number of shares acquired, divided by
-- the number of issued shares of the class or series immediately before the acquisition.
@export How much must my corporation deduct from the stated capital account when it acquires its own shares, in dollars (s 39(1))?
GIVEN `the stated capital of the class or series, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the stated capital of the shares of that class or series, in dollars?
      `the number of shares acquired` IS A NUMBER @desc How many shares (or fractions of shares) of the class or series are purchased, redeemed or otherwise acquired?
      `the number of issued shares before the acquisition` IS A NUMBER @desc How many shares of that class or series were issued immediately before the acquisition?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much must my corporation deduct from the stated capital account when it acquires its own shares` IS
    `the amount to deduct from the stated capital account on an acquisition within s 39(1)` `the stated capital of the class or series, in dollars` `the number of shares acquired` `the number of issued shares before the acquisition`

-- s 39(2). A corporation shall deduct the amount of a payment made to a shareholder under paragraph 241(3)(g)
-- from the stated capital account for the class or series in respect of which the payment was made.
@export What is the stated capital account balance after a payment to a shareholder under paragraph 241(3)(g), in dollars (s 39(2))?
GIVEN `the balance of the account, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the balance of the stated capital account for the class or series, in dollars?
      `the payment, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the payment made to a shareholder under paragraph 241(3)(g), in dollars?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the stated capital account balance after a payment to a shareholder under paragraph 241(3)(g)` IS
    `the balance of the stated capital account after the payment within s 39(2)` `the balance of the account, in dollars` `the payment, in dollars`

-- s 39(3). A corporation shall adjust its stated capital account or accounts in accordance with any special
-- resolution referred to in subsection 38(2).
@export Must my corporation adjust its stated capital accounts in accordance with our special resolution (s 39(3))?
GIVEN `we passed a special resolution under subsection 38(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a special resolution referred to in subsection 38(2) been passed?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my corporation adjust its stated capital accounts in accordance with our special resolution` IF
    `the corporation must adjust its stated capital accounts in accordance with the special resolution within s 39(3)` `we passed a special resolution under subsection 38(2)`

-- s 39(4). On a conversion of issued shares into shares of another class or series, or a change under s 173, 191
-- or 241, the corporation shall (a) deduct from the stated capital account of the class or series converted or
-- changed the stated capital of those shares multiplied by the number converted or changed, divided by the
-- number of issued shares immediately before; and (b) add that result, and any additional consideration
-- received, to the account of the class or series into which they were converted or changed.
@export How much must my corporation deduct from the stated capital account on a conversion or change of shares, in dollars (s 39(4)(a))?
GIVEN `the stated capital of the class or series, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the stated capital of the shares of the class or series converted or changed, in dollars?
      `the number of shares converted or changed` IS A NUMBER @desc How many shares of that class or series are converted or changed?
      `the number of issued shares before the conversion` IS A NUMBER @desc How many shares of that class or series were issued immediately before the conversion or change?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much must my corporation deduct from the stated capital account on a conversion or change of shares` IS
    `the amount to deduct on a conversion or change within s 39(4)(a)` `the stated capital of the class or series, in dollars` `the number of shares converted or changed` `the number of issued shares before the conversion`

@export How much must my corporation add to the stated capital account of the new class or series on a conversion or change of shares, in dollars (s 39(4)(b))?
GIVEN `the stated capital of the class or series, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the stated capital of the shares of the class or series converted or changed, in dollars?
      `the number of shares converted or changed` IS A NUMBER @desc How many shares of that class or series are converted or changed?
      `the number of issued shares before the conversion` IS A NUMBER @desc How many shares of that class or series were issued immediately before the conversion or change?
      `the additional consideration received, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What additional consideration was received pursuant to the conversion or change, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much must my corporation add to the stated capital account of the new class or series on a conversion or change of shares` IS
    `the amount to add on a conversion or change within s 39(4)(b)` (`the amount to deduct on a conversion or change within s 39(4)(a)` `the stated capital of the class or series, in dollars` `the number of shares converted or changed` `the number of issued shares before the conversion`) `the additional consideration received, in dollars`

-- s 39(5). For the purposes of subsection (4) and subject to its articles, where a corporation issues two classes
-- of shares each convertible into the other, the stated capital attributable to a share in either class is the
-- aggregate of the stated capital of both classes divided by the number of issued shares of both classes
-- immediately before the conversion.
@export Does my corporation have two classes of interconvertible shares (s 39(5))?
GIVEN `we issue two classes of shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the corporation issue two classes of shares?
      `each class can be converted into the other` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there attached to each class a right to convert a share of the one class into a share of the other?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my corporation have two classes of interconvertible shares` IF
    `the corporation has two classes of convertible shares referred to in s 39(5)` `we issue two classes of shares` `each class can be converted into the other`

@export How much stated capital is attributable to one of my corporation's interconvertible shares, in dollars (s 39(5))?
GIVEN `our articles provide otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the articles provide otherwise?
      `the stated capital of the first class, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the stated capital of the first class, in dollars?
      `the stated capital of the second class, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the stated capital of the second class, in dollars?
      `the number of issued shares of the first class` IS A NUMBER @desc How many shares of the first class were issued immediately before the conversion?
      `the number of issued shares of the second class` IS A NUMBER @desc How many shares of the second class were issued immediately before the conversion?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much stated capital is attributable to one of my corporation's interconvertible shares` IS
    `the stated capital attributable to a share in either class within s 39(5)` `our articles provide otherwise` `the stated capital of the first class, in dollars` `the stated capital of the second class, in dollars` `the number of issued shares of the first class` `the number of issued shares of the second class`

-- s 39(6). Shares or fractions of shares issued by a corporation and purchased, redeemed or otherwise acquired by
-- it shall be cancelled or, if the articles limit the number of authorized shares, may be restored to the status
-- of authorized but unissued shares of the class.
@export What becomes of shares my corporation has bought back, redeemed or otherwise acquired (s 39(6))?
GIVEN `my articles limit the authorized shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the articles limit the number of authorized shares?
GIVETH A `What becomes of shares a corporation has acquired (s 39(6))`
DECIDE `What becomes of shares my corporation has bought back redeemed or otherwise acquired` IS
    `what becomes of the acquired shares within s 39(6)` `my articles limit the authorized shares`

-- s 39(7). For the purposes of section 39, a corporation holding shares in itself as permitted by subsections
-- 31(1) and (2) is deemed not to have purchased, redeemed or otherwise acquired them.
@export Is my corporation deemed not to have acquired shares it holds in itself under section 31 (s 39(7))?
GIVEN `we hold the shares in ourselves as section 31(1) or (2) permits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the corporation hold the shares in itself as permitted by subsection 31(1) or (2)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my corporation deemed not to have acquired shares it holds in itself under section 31` IF
    `the corporation is deemed not to have purchased, redeemed or otherwise acquired the shares for the purposes of s 39 within s 39(7)` `we hold the shares in ourselves as section 31(1) or (2) permits`

-- s 39(8). A corporation holding shares in itself as permitted by paragraph 32(1)(a) is deemed not to have
-- acquired them when they were acquired, but those still held at the expiration of two years (and shares into
-- which they were converted and held under paragraph 32(1)(b), at the expiration of two years after the shares
-- from which they were converted were acquired) are deemed to have been acquired at the expiration of the two
-- years.
@export On what day are the shares my corporation holds under paragraph 32(1)(a) deemed to have been acquired (s 39(8))?
GIVEN `the shares are held under paragraph 32(1)(a) or (b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the shares held as permitted by paragraph 32(1)(a), or are they shares into which such shares were converted and held under paragraph 32(1)(b)?
      `the day they were acquired` IS A DATE @desc On what day were the shares (or the shares from which they were converted) acquired?
      `we still hold them after two years` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the corporation still hold the shares at the expiration of the two years?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `On what day are the shares my corporation holds under paragraph 32(1)(a) deemed to have been acquired` IS
    `the day the shares are deemed to have been acquired within s 39(8)` `the shares are held under paragraph 32(1)(a) or (b)` `the day they were acquired` `we still hold them after two years`

-- s 39(9). Shares issued and converted into shares of another class or series, or changed under s 173, 191 or
-- 241, become issued shares of the class or series into which they were converted or changed.
@export Do my shares become issued shares of the class or series they were converted or changed into (s 39(9))?
GIVEN `my shares were converted or changed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were your issued shares converted into shares of another class or series, or changed under section 173, 191 or 241 into shares of another class or series?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do my shares become issued shares of the class or series they were converted or changed into` IF
    `the shares become issued shares of the class or series into which they were converted or changed within s 39(9)` `my shares were converted or changed`

-- s 39(10). Where the articles limit the number of authorized shares of a class and issued shares of it have
-- become issued shares of another class or series, the number of unissued shares of the first class shall,
-- unless the articles otherwise provide, be increased by the number that became shares of another class or
-- series.
@export How many unissued shares does the first class have after a conversion or change (s 39(10))?
GIVEN `the articles limit the first class` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the articles limit the number of authorized shares of the first class?
      `the articles otherwise provide` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the articles otherwise provide?
      `the unissued shares before` IS A NUMBER @desc How many unissued shares of the first class were there before the change?
      `the number that became shares of another class` IS A NUMBER @desc How many shares became shares of another class or series?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How many unissued shares does the first class have after a conversion or change` IS
    `the number of unissued shares of the first class after the change within s 39(10)` `the articles limit the first class` `the articles otherwise provide` `the unissued shares before` `the number that became shares of another class`

-- s 39(11). Debt obligations issued, pledged, hypothecated or deposited by a corporation are not redeemed by
-- reason only that the indebtedness they evidence, or in respect of which they were issued, pledged,
-- hypothecated or deposited, is repaid.
@export Are debt obligations redeemed just because the debt they evidence is repaid (s 39(11))?
GIVEN `the indebtedness is repaid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the indebtedness evidenced by the debt obligations (or in respect of which they were issued, pledged, hypothecated or deposited) been repaid?
      `they are redeemed on another ground` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the debt obligations redeemed on some ground other than that the indebtedness is repaid?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are debt obligations redeemed just because the debt they evidence is repaid` IF
    `the debt obligations are redeemed within s 39(11)` `the indebtedness is repaid` `they are redeemed on another ground`

-- s 39(12). Debt obligations purchased, redeemed or otherwise acquired by the corporation may be cancelled or,
-- subject to any applicable trust indenture or other agreement, may be reissued, pledged or hypothecated to
-- secure any obligation then existing or later incurred; and that acquisition and reissue is not a cancellation.
@export May my corporation reissue, pledge or hypothecate debt obligations it has acquired (s 39(12))?
GIVEN `a trust indenture or agreement prohibits it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does an applicable trust indenture or other agreement prohibit the reissue, pledge or hypothecation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my corporation reissue pledge or hypothecate debt obligations it has acquired` IF
    `the corporation may reissue, pledge or hypothecate the acquired debt obligations within s 39(12)` `a trust indenture or agreement prohibits it`

@export Is the acquisition and reissue of debt obligations a cancellation of them (s 39(12))?
GIVEN `they were acquired and then reissued pledged or hypothecated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the debt obligations acquired by the corporation and then reissued, pledged or hypothecated?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the acquisition and reissue of debt obligations a cancellation of them` IF
    `the acquisition and reissue, pledge or hypothecation is a cancellation of the debt obligations within s 39(12)` `they were acquired and then reissued pledged or hypothecated`

-- s 40(1). A corporation shall fulfil its obligations under a contract to buy shares of the corporation, except
-- if it can prove that enforcement of the contract would put it in breach of any of sections 34 to 36.
@export Must the corporation fulfil its contract to buy my shares (s 40(1))?
GIVEN `the corporation can prove that enforcement would breach sections 34 to 36` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can the corporation prove that enforcement of the contract would put it in breach of section 34, 35 or 36?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the corporation fulfil its contract to buy my shares` IF
    `the corporation must fulfil its obligations under the contract to buy shares within s 40(1)` `the corporation can prove that enforcement would breach sections 34 to 36`

-- s 40(2). Until the corporation has fulfilled all its obligations under the contract, the other party retains the
-- status of claimant entitled to be paid as soon as the corporation is lawfully able to do so or, in a
-- liquidation, to be ranked subordinate to the rights of creditors and of holders of any class whose rights
-- were in priority to those of the class being purchased, but in priority to the rights of other shareholders.
@export Am I entitled to be paid under my contract to sell my shares to the corporation (s 40(2))?
GIVEN `the corporation has fulfilled all its obligations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the corporation fulfilled all its obligations under the contract?
      `the corporation is lawfully able to pay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation lawfully able to pay?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I entitled to be paid under my contract to sell my shares to the corporation` IF
    `the other party is entitled to be paid within s 40(2)` `the corporation has fulfilled all its obligations` `the corporation is lawfully able to pay`

@export In a liquidation, do I rank ahead of this person under my contract to sell shares to the corporation (s 40(2))?
GIVEN `the person` IS A `Person ranked against the claimant in a liquidation (s 40(2))` @desc Who is the other person?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `In a liquidation do I rank ahead of this person under my contract to sell shares to the corporation` IS
    `the claimant ranks in priority to the person in a liquidation within s 40(2)` `the person`

-- s 41. The directors may authorize the corporation to pay a reasonable commission to any person in
-- consideration of the person's purchasing or agreeing to purchase shares of the corporation from the
-- corporation or from any other person, or procuring or agreeing to procure purchasers for any such shares.
@export May the directors authorize the corporation to pay a commission for the sale of its shares (s 41)?
GIVEN `the commission is reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the commission reasonable?
      `it is for buying or procuring purchasers of shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it in consideration of the person's purchasing or agreeing to purchase shares of the corporation from the corporation or from any other person, or procuring or agreeing to procure purchasers for any such shares?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the directors authorize the corporation to pay a commission for the sale of its shares` IF
    `the directors may authorize the corporation to pay the commission within s 41` `the commission is reasonable` `it is for buying or procuring purchasers of shares`

-- s 42. A corporation shall not declare or pay a dividend if there are reasonable grounds for believing that (a)
-- it is, or would after the payment be, unable to pay its liabilities as they become due, or (b) the realizable
-- value of its assets would thereby be less than the aggregate of its liabilities and stated capital of all
-- classes. (An open-end mutual fund has no stated capital for this purpose -- fork cb1-F9.)
@export Is my corporation forbidden to declare or pay a dividend (s 42)?
GIVEN `there are grounds to believe we cannot pay our debts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are there reasonable grounds for believing that the corporation is, or would after the payment be, unable to pay its liabilities as they become due?
      `the realizable value of our assets after the payment, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What would the realizable value of the corporation's assets be after the payment, in dollars?
      `our liabilities, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What are the corporation's liabilities, in dollars?
      `our stated capital of all classes, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the stated capital of all classes of the corporation, in dollars?
      `we are an open-end mutual fund` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation an open-end mutual fund?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my corporation forbidden to declare or pay a dividend` IF
    `the corporation is forbidden to declare or pay a dividend within s 42` `the solvency facts`
    WHERE
        `the solvency facts` MEANS `Facts for a solvency test in Part V` WITH
            -- Placeholders: the s 42 rule does not read the two amounts owed to holders of other shares.
            `reasonable grounds exist for believing that the corporation is, or would after the step be, unable to pay its liabilities as they become due` IS `there are grounds to believe we cannot pay our debts`
            `realizable value of the corporation's assets after the step, in dollars` IS `the realizable value of our assets after the payment, in dollars`
            `liabilities of the corporation, in dollars` IS `our liabilities, in dollars`
            `stated capital of all classes, in dollars` IS `our stated capital of all classes, in dollars`
            `amount required, on a redemption or in a liquidation, to pay the holders of shares that must be paid before the shares to be acquired and not included in the liabilities, in dollars` IS 0
            `amount required, on a redemption or in a liquidation, to pay the holders of shares that must be paid rateably with or before the shares to be acquired and not included in the liabilities, in dollars` IS 0
            `the corporation is an open-end mutual fund` IS `we are an open-end mutual fund`

-- s 43(1). A corporation may pay a dividend by issuing fully paid shares of the corporation and, subject to
-- section 42, may pay a dividend in money or property.
@export May my corporation pay a dividend in this form (s 43(1))?
GIVEN `the form` IS A `Form of a dividend (s 43(1))` @desc In what form do you want to pay the dividend?
      `there are grounds to believe we cannot pay our debts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are there reasonable grounds for believing that the corporation is, or would after the payment be, unable to pay its liabilities as they become due?
      `the realizable value of our assets after the payment, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What would the realizable value of the corporation's assets be after the payment, in dollars?
      `our liabilities, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What are the corporation's liabilities, in dollars?
      `our stated capital of all classes, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the stated capital of all classes of the corporation, in dollars?
      `we are an open-end mutual fund` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation an open-end mutual fund?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my corporation pay a dividend in this form` IF
    `the corporation may pay the dividend in that form within s 43(1)` `the form` (`the corporation is forbidden to declare or pay a dividend within s 42` `the solvency facts`)
    WHERE
        `the solvency facts` MEANS `Facts for a solvency test in Part V` WITH
            -- Placeholders: the s 42 rule does not read the two amounts owed to holders of other shares.
            `reasonable grounds exist for believing that the corporation is, or would after the step be, unable to pay its liabilities as they become due` IS `there are grounds to believe we cannot pay our debts`
            `realizable value of the corporation's assets after the step, in dollars` IS `the realizable value of our assets after the payment, in dollars`
            `liabilities of the corporation, in dollars` IS `our liabilities, in dollars`
            `stated capital of all classes, in dollars` IS `our stated capital of all classes, in dollars`
            `amount required, on a redemption or in a liquidation, to pay the holders of shares that must be paid before the shares to be acquired and not included in the liabilities, in dollars` IS 0
            `amount required, on a redemption or in a liquidation, to pay the holders of shares that must be paid rateably with or before the shares to be acquired and not included in the liabilities, in dollars` IS 0
            `the corporation is an open-end mutual fund` IS `we are an open-end mutual fund`

-- s 43(2). If shares are issued in payment of a dividend, the declared amount of the dividend stated as an amount
-- of money shall be added to the stated capital account for the class or series issued.
@export How much must my corporation add to the stated capital account when it pays a dividend in shares, in dollars (s 43(2))?
GIVEN `shares are issued in payment of the dividend` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are shares of the corporation issued in payment of the dividend?
      `the declared amount of the dividend, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the declared amount of the dividend, stated as an amount of money, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much must my corporation add to the stated capital account when it pays a dividend in shares` IS
    `the amount to add to the stated capital account for the class or series issued within s 43(2)` `shares are issued in payment of the dividend` `the declared amount of the dividend, in dollars`

-- s 45(1). The shareholders of a corporation are not, as shareholders, liable for any liability, act or default
-- of the corporation except under subsection 38(4), 118(4) or (5), 146(5) or 226(4) or (5).
@export Am I, as a shareholder, protected from liability for the corporation's liabilities, acts and defaults (s 45(1))?
GIVEN `the basis of the claim` IS A `Basis on which a shareholder is said to be liable for the corporation's liability, act or default (s 45(1))` @desc On what basis is it said that you are liable?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I as a shareholder protected from liability for the corporation's liabilities acts and defaults` IF
    `section 45(1) shields the shareholder from the liability within s 45(1)` `the basis of the claim`

-- s 45(2). Subject to subsection 49(8), the articles may provide that the corporation has a lien or hypothec on
-- a share registered in the name of a shareholder or the shareholder's personal representative for a debt of that
-- shareholder to the corporation, including an amount unpaid in respect of a share issued by a body corporate
-- on the date it was continued under the Act.
@export May the articles give the corporation a lien or hypothec on my shares (s 45(2))?
GIVEN `the share is registered in my name or my personal representative's` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the share registered in the name of the shareholder or the shareholder's personal representative?
      `the lien secures a debt I owe the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the lien or hypothec for a debt of that shareholder to the corporation (including an amount unpaid on a share issued by a body corporate on the date it was continued)?
      -- out of range: section 49(8) (piece cb2)
      `subsection 49(8) forbids it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does subsection 49(8) forbid it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the articles give the corporation a lien or hypothec on my shares` IF
    `the articles may provide that the corporation has a lien or hypothec on the share within s 45(2)` `the share is registered in my name or my personal representative's` `the lien secures a debt I owe the corporation` `subsection 49(8) forbids it`

-- s 45(3). A corporation may enforce a lien or hypothec referred to in subsection (2) in accordance with its
-- by-laws.
@export May the corporation enforce a lien or hypothec on my shares (s 45(3))?
GIVEN `a lien or hypothec under subsection 45(2) exists` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a lien or hypothec referred to in subsection 45(2) exist on the share?
      `the enforcement follows the by-laws` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the enforcement in accordance with the by-laws of the corporation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the corporation enforce a lien or hypothec on my shares` IF
    `the corporation may enforce the lien or hypothec within s 45(3)` `a lien or hypothec under subsection 45(2) exists` `the enforcement follows the by-laws`

§§ `Constrained shares sold by the corporation (Part VI, s 46 and s 47)`

-- This group arises only where the corporation has constraints on the issue, transfer or ownership of its
-- shares and sells constrained shares: the form may ask "Has your corporation sold, or is it selling, shares
-- that are owned contrary to the constraints on its shares?" before showing it.

-- s 46(1). A corporation that has constraints on the issue, transfer or ownership of its shares may, for any of
-- three purposes, sell, under the prescribed conditions and after giving the prescribed notice, as if it were the
-- owner, any of those constrained shares that are owned, or that the directors determine in the prescribed
-- manner may be owned, contrary to the constraints.
@export May my corporation sell my constrained shares as if it were their owner (s 46(1))?
GIVEN `the purpose` IS A `Purpose of a sale of constrained shares (s 46(1))` @desc For what purpose does the corporation want to sell the shares?
      `the corporation has constraints on its shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the corporation have constraints on the issue, transfer or ownership of its shares of the class or series?
      -- out of range: the regulations (not among the sources)
      `the shares are owned contrary to the constraints` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the shares owned, or have the directors determined in the prescribed manner that they may be owned, contrary to the constraints?
      -- out of range: the regulations (not among the sources)
      `the prescribed conditions and notice have been met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the prescribed conditions met and has the prescribed notice been given?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my corporation sell my constrained shares as if it were their owner` IF
    `the corporation may sell the constrained shares as if it were their owner within s 46(1)` `the purpose` `the corporation has constraints on its shares` `the shares are owned contrary to the constraints` `the prescribed conditions and notice have been met`

-- s 46(2). Where shares are to be sold under subsection (1), the directors shall select the shares for sale in
-- good faith and in a manner that is not unfairly prejudicial to, and does not unfairly disregard the interests
-- of, the holders of the shares in the constrained class or series taken as a whole.
@export Have the directors selected the shares for sale as the Act requires (s 46(2))?
GIVEN `the directors selected in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the directors select the shares for sale in good faith?
      `the selection is unfairly prejudicial` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the selection unfairly prejudicial to the holders of the shares in the constrained class or series taken as a whole?
      `the selection unfairly disregards the holders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the selection unfairly disregard the interests of those holders?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have the directors selected the shares for sale as the Act requires` IF
    `the directors have complied with the duty in selecting the shares for sale within s 46(2)` `the directors selected in good faith` `the selection is unfairly prejudicial` `the selection unfairly disregards the holders`

-- s 46(3). If shares are sold under subsection (1), the owner immediately before the sale is divested of their
-- interest or right in the shares, and the person who would otherwise be the registered owner, or who satisfies
-- the corporation that they could properly be treated as the registered owner or holder under section 51,
-- is entitled from the time of the sale to receive only the net proceeds of the sale, with income earned on
-- the proceeds from the beginning of the month next following the corporation's receipt of them, less taxes and
-- the costs of administration of a trust fund constituted under subsection 47(1).
@export Am I divested of my interest in my shares when the corporation sells them (s 46(3))?
GIVEN `the corporation sold the shares under subsection 46(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the shares sold by the corporation under subsection 46(1)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I divested of my interest in my shares when the corporation sells them` IF
    `the owner immediately before the sale is divested of their interest or right in the shares within s 46(3)` `the corporation sold the shares under subsection 46(1)`

@export Am I entitled to receive only the net proceeds of the sale of my shares (s 46(3))?
GIVEN `the corporation sold the shares under subsection 46(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the shares sold by the corporation under subsection 46(1)?
      `I would otherwise be the registered owner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc But for the sale, would you be the registered owner of the shares?
      -- out of range: section 51 (piece cb2)
      `I satisfied the corporation I could be treated as the holder under section 51` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you satisfied the corporation that, but for the sale, you could properly be treated as the registered owner or registered holder of the shares under section 51?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I entitled to receive only the net proceeds of the sale of my shares` IF
    `the person is entitled to receive only the net proceeds of the sale within s 46(3)` `the corporation sold the shares under subsection 46(1)` `I would otherwise be the registered owner` `I satisfied the corporation I could be treated as the holder under section 51`

@export How much am I entitled to receive from the sale of my shares, in dollars (s 46(3))?
GIVEN `the net proceeds of the sale, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What were the net proceeds of the sale, in dollars?
      `the income earned on the proceeds, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What income was earned on the proceeds from the beginning of the month next following the date the corporation received them, in dollars?
      `the taxes on the proceeds, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What are the taxes on the proceeds, in dollars?
      `the costs of administering the trust fund, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What are the costs of administration of a trust fund constituted under subsection 47(1) in relation to the constitution of the fund, in dollars?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much am I entitled to receive from the sale of my shares` IS
    `what the person who would otherwise be the registered owner receives within s 46(3)` `the net proceeds of the sale, in dollars` `the income earned on the proceeds, in dollars` `the taxes on the proceeds, in dollars` `the costs of administering the trust fund, in dollars`

-- s 46(4). Subsections 51(4) to (6) apply to the person entitled under subsection (3) to receive the proceeds, as
-- if the proceeds were a security and the person were a registered holder or owner of it.
@export Do subsections 51(4) to (6) apply to me as the person entitled to the proceeds of the sale (s 46(4))?
GIVEN `I am entitled to the proceeds under subsection 46(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled under subsection 46(3) to receive the proceeds of a sale of shares under subsection 46(1)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do subsections 51(4) to (6) apply to me as the person entitled to the proceeds of the sale` IF
    `subsections 51(4) to (6) apply to the person as if the proceeds were a security and the person were a registered holder or owner within s 46(4)` `I am entitled to the proceeds under subsection 46(3)`

-- s 47(1). The proceeds of a sale under subsection 46(1) constitute a trust fund in the hands of the corporation
-- for the benefit of the person entitled under subsection 46(3), may be commingled with other such trust funds,
-- and shall be invested in the prescribed manner.
@export Do the proceeds of the sale of my shares form a trust fund held for me (s 47(1))?
GIVEN `the proceeds are from a sale under subsection 46(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they the proceeds of a sale by the corporation under subsection 46(1)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do the proceeds of the sale of my shares form a trust fund held for me` IF
    `the proceeds constitute a trust fund in the hands of the corporation within s 47(1)` `the proceeds are from a sale under subsection 46(1)`

@export Has the corporation invested the trust fund as the Act requires (s 47(1))?
GIVEN
      -- out of range: the regulations (not among the sources)
      `the fund is invested in the prescribed manner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the fund invested in the manner that the regulations prescribe?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has the corporation invested the trust fund as the Act requires` IF
    `the trust fund has been invested as s 47(1) requires` `the fund is invested in the prescribed manner`

-- s 47(2). Reasonable costs of administration of a trust fund may be deducted from the trust fund and any income
-- earned on it.
@export May the corporation deduct its costs from the trust fund held for me (s 47(2))?
GIVEN `the costs are reasonable costs of administration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the costs reasonable costs of administration of the trust fund?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the corporation deduct its costs from the trust fund held for me` IF
    `the corporation may deduct the costs from the trust fund and any income earned thereon within s 47(2)` `the costs are reasonable costs of administration`

-- s 47(3). Subject to s 47, a corporation may transfer the trust fund, and its administration, to a trust company
-- in Canada registered as such under the laws of Canada or a province, and is thereupon discharged of all
-- further liability in respect of the trust fund.
@export May the corporation transfer the trust fund held for me to a trust company (s 47(3))?
GIVEN `the transferee is a registered trust company in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the transferee a trust company in Canada registered as such under the laws of Canada or a province?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the corporation transfer the trust fund held for me to a trust company` IF
    `the corporation may transfer the trust fund and its administration to the transferee within s 47(3)` `the transferee is a registered trust company in Canada`

@export Is the corporation discharged of liability for the trust fund held for me after transferring it (s 47(3))?
GIVEN `the corporation transferred the fund and its administration to a trust company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the corporation transfer the trust fund, and the administration of it, to a trust company under subsection 47(3)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the corporation discharged of liability for the trust fund held for me after transferring it` IF
    `the corporation is discharged of all further liability in respect of the trust fund within s 47(3)` `the corporation transferred the fund and its administration to a trust company`

-- s 47(4). A receipt signed by a person entitled under subsection 46(3) to receive the proceeds is a complete
-- discharge of the corporation and of any trust company to which the fund is transferred, in respect of the
-- trust fund and income paid to that person.
@export Is my signed receipt a complete discharge of the corporation and any trust company (s 47(4))?
GIVEN `the receipt is signed by the person entitled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the receipt signed by a person entitled under subsection 46(3) to receive the proceeds of the sale?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my signed receipt a complete discharge of the corporation and any trust company` IF
    `the receipt is a complete discharge of the corporation and of any trust company within s 47(4)` `the receipt is signed by the person entitled`

-- s 47(5). A trust fund, with its income, less taxes and costs of administration, that has not been claimed by
-- the person entitled under subsection 46(3) for ten years after the date of the sale vests in Her Majesty in
-- right of Canada.
@export By what day must I claim the trust fund before it vests in the Crown (s 47(5))?
GIVEN `the date of the sale` IS A DATE @desc On what date were the shares sold?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what day must I claim the trust fund before it vests in the Crown` IS
    `the last day the fund can be claimed before it vests in the Crown within s 47(5)` `the date of the sale`

@export Has the trust fund held for me vested in the Crown on this day (s 47(5))?
GIVEN `the date of the sale` IS A DATE @desc On what date were the shares sold?
      `the fund has been claimed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the fund been claimed by a person entitled under subsection 46(3) to receive the proceeds?
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you want to know whether the fund has vested?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has the trust fund held for me vested in the Crown on this day` IF
    `the fund has vested in Her Majesty in right of Canada on the day within s 47(5)` `the date of the sale` `the fund has been claimed` `the day I am asking about`

-- s 47(6). Sections 3 to 5 of the Escheats Act apply in respect of a trust fund that vests in Her Majesty in right
-- of Canada under subsection (5).
@export Do sections 3 to 5 of the Escheats Act apply to a trust fund that has vested in the Crown (s 47(6))?
GIVEN `the fund has vested under subsection 47(5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the fund vested in Her Majesty in right of Canada under subsection 47(5)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do sections 3 to 5 of the Escheats Act apply to a trust fund that has vested in the Crown` IF
    `sections 3 to 5 of the Escheats Act apply to the fund within s 47(6)` `the fund has vested under subsection 47(5)`

